{"parentUuid":"59a26a2c-40cf-442b-9eb5-30eb36cb89ee","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"5b41bf5b-39b7-47b2-b1be-8bc0501d2b90","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014pJFQERTqNAMhggRKFuDNe","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t// Organic 2D force-graph drop-in renderer.\n2\t//\n3\t// Slots into `memoray.lineage_graph`, `kg3d.synoptic_web`, and\n4\t// `codegraph.canvas` via the same `options.renderer = { mount, update,\n5\t// dispose }` hook that `three_renderer` uses. The widget cores stay\n6\t// dependency-free (default 2D SVG); callers that want the living, organic\n7\t// graph — the Memo-Ray look (force-simulated motion, node glow, animated\n8\t// trace particles on the active path, a corner minimap) — pass an instance\n9\t// returned by `createForceGraph2DRenderer()` and the widget never learns the\n10\t// graphing library exists.\n11\t//\n12\t// ## Offline by design\n13\t//\n14\t// Unlike `three_renderer` (which lazy-loads `3d-force-graph` from a CDN), the\n15\t// 2D library is **vendored locally** at `vendor/force-graph.module.js` (a\n16\t// self-contained esbuild bundle of vasturiano/force-graph with every d3 /\n17\t// lodash dependency inlined — zero bare imports, see vendor/README.md). The\n18\t// default loader dynamic-imports that local path, so the renderer works with\n19\t// no network at all. The import is still lazy (only on first mount) so pages\n20\t// that never open a graph pay nothing.\n21\t//\n22\t// Tests inject `options.loader = () => Promise<ForceGraph>` so the node runner\n23\t// never touches the vendored bundle or the DOM.\n24\t//\n25\t// ## Layout contract (shared with three_renderer)\n26\t//\n27\t//   • `memoray.lineage_graph` → positions carry { x, y, depth, node }\n28\t//   • `kg3d.synoptic_web`     → positions carry { x, y, radius, layer, color, node }\n29\t//   • `codegraph.canvas`      → positions carry { x, y, radius, type, color, node }\n30\t//\n31\t// `layoutToGraphData(layout, physics)` normalises all three into the\n32\t// `{ nodes, links }` shape force-graph expects. Lineage positions carry no\n33\t// colour/radius, so colour is derived from the node's `type` via the Memo-Ray\n34\t// palette and size from a per-type default. `physics === \"pinned\"` fixes\n35\t// fx/fy (frozen layout); `\"fluid\"` only seeds x/y and lets the simulation run\n36\t// (the organic motion).\n37\t//\n38\t// ## Click / hover\n39\t//\n40\t// Both conventions are honoured: the per-mount `props.onSelect(id)` used by\n41\t// the SVG renderers, and the factory `options.onNodeClick(id, node)` used by\n42\t// the Bridge's `makeThreeRenderer`-style wiring. Whichever is present fires.\n43\t\n44\tconst DEFAULT_VENDOR_URL = new URL(\"./vendor/force-graph.module.js\", import.meta.url).href;\n45\tconst DEFAULT_BACKGROUND = \"transparent\";\n46\t\n47\t// Memo-Ray organic palette, by node type (mirrors OrganicGraph.jsx PALETTE\n48\t// and lineage_graph's NODE_TYPE_COLORS — earth tones, sage/moss/golden).\n49\tconst PALETTE = {\n50\t  \"User Input\": \"#b8a898\",\n51\t  Thought: \"#8b9c8b\",\n52\t  Message: \"#8b9c8b\",\n53\t  \"Tool Call\": \"#6a8a6a\",\n54\t  \"Tool Result\": \"#6a8a6a\",\n55\t  Artifact: \"#8a9aa4\",\n56\t  Session: \"#c4a882\",\n57\t  \"System Init\": \"#5a6a5e\",\n58\t  Error: \"#c47a6a\"\n59\t};\n60\tconst DEFAULT_NODE_COLOR = \"#6b7378\";"}]},"uuid":"d8270588-499d-46bd-b9bf-e4ccbbac0435","timestamp":"2026-07-03T18:56:38.953Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"prime-silo\\app\\L0\\_all\\mod\\_prime_silo\\widgets\\force_graph_2d\\index.js","content":"// Organic 2D force-graph drop-in renderer.\n//\n// Slots into `memoray.lineage_graph`, `kg3d.synoptic_web`, and\n// `codegraph.canvas` via the same `options.renderer = { mount, update,\n// dispose }` hook that `three_renderer` uses. The widget cores stay\n// dependency-free (default 2D SVG); callers that want the living, organic\n// graph — the Memo-Ray look (force-simulated motion, node glow, animated\n// trace particles on the active path, a corner minimap) — pass an instance\n// returned by `createForceGraph2DRenderer()` and the widget never learns the\n// graphing library exists.\n//\n// ## Offline by design\n//\n// Unlike `three_renderer` (which lazy-loads `3d-force-graph` from a CDN), the\n// 2D library is **vendored locally** at `vendor/force-graph.module.js` (a\n// self-contained esbuild bundle of vasturiano/force-graph with every d3 /\n// lodash dependency inlined — zero bare imports, see vendor/README.md). The\n// default loader dynamic-imports that local path, so the renderer works with\n// no network at all. The import is still lazy (only on first mount) so pages\n// that never open a graph pay nothing.\n//\n// Tests inject `options.loader = () => Promise<ForceGraph>` so the node runner\n// never touches the vendored bundle or the DOM.\n//\n// ## Layout contract (shared with three_renderer)\n//\n//   • `memoray.lineage_graph` → positions carry { x, y, depth, node }\n//   • `kg3d.synoptic_web`     → positions carry { x, y, radius, layer, color, node }\n//   • `codegraph.canvas`      → positions carry { x, y, radius, type, color, node }\n//\n// `layoutToGraphData(layout, physics)` normalises all three into the\n// `{ nodes, links }` shape force-graph expects. Lineage positions carry no\n// colour/radius, so colour is derived from the node's `type` via the Memo-Ray\n// palette and size from a per-type default. `physics === \"pinned\"` fixes\n// fx/fy (frozen layout); `\"fluid\"` only seeds x/y and lets the simulation run\n// (the organic motion).\n//\n// ## Click / hover\n//\n// Both conventions are honoured: the per-mount `props.onSelect(id)` used by\n// the SVG renderers, and the factory `options.onNodeClick(id, node)` used by\n// the Bridge's `makeThreeRenderer`-style wiring. Whichever is present fires.\n\nconst DEFAULT_VENDOR_URL = new URL(\"./vendor/force-graph.module.js\", import.meta.url).href;\nconst DEFAULT_BACKGROUND = \"transparent\";\n\n// Memo-Ray orga