ithout await) + added `test_large_graph_metrics_are_bounded`.\n25\t\n26\t**Bundle rebuilt + installed (2026-06-23/24).** Rebuilt win-unpacked (`npm run desktop:localtest`, v1.2.14) — ships the shell/skill fixes (benny-pilot helpers, documents branch, SKILL.md), verified inside `dist/desktop/windows/win-unpacked/resources/app/...`. NOTE: the runtime bundle is NOT packed into win-unpacked (build.files excludes packaging/runtime-bundle; desktop-builder.js:523-530 — it's a separate fetched archive, the v1.2.8 Defender/EBUSY lesson). Built the proper runtime archive via `pack-runtime-bundle.js` → `dist/runtime-bundle/runtime-bundle-win32-x64.tar.gz` (607MB, app_version 1.2.14, carries the kg3d fix via copyBennySource). Then INSTALLED it into `AppData/Roaming/space-agent/runtime-bundle` (extracted + wrote `.runtime-bundle.json` marker app_version 1.2.14) — verified python/site/benny/neo4j/jre present and all 3 kg3d-fix files present. Pending: user relaunches Space Agent.exe.\n27\t\n28\t**Build-tooling bug fixed (assemble-runtime-bundle.js + pack-runtime-bundle.js):** the packer called `tar` unqualified; on Windows with Git installed, Git's GNU tar shadows bsdtar on PATH and misreads a `C:\\...` archive path as a remote host (\"Cannot connect to C: resolve failed\"), crashing the pack. Added `tarBin()` pinning win32 to `System32\\tar.exe` (bsdtar). Used in both extract and create-tar calls.\n29\t\n30\t**Shipped as v1.2.15 (2026-06-24).** Committed (6407a1e) the kg3d fix + benny-pilot skill + tar build-tooling fix + test updates (and dropped stray runtime/failed_llm_output_*.txt). `node scripts/manage-release.js patch` → 1.2.15 (commit 3e2a895, tag v1.2.15). Pushed main THEN tag (the critical order). Release-desktop.yml triggered (run 28083792517). Caveat: local pytest release gates (tests/release, tests/portability) were NOT run — pytest isn't in the bundled python or repo .venv; relied on CI + the per-change tests verified by hand. manage-release.js only stages package.js