{"parentUuid":"093e12e1-8fca-4550-8f49-d9e1799391a8","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"777c960c-379c-49f7-97e9-1009775c30a7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PUBhrS5oHuutcdxhS524H8","type":"tool_result","content":"The file C:\\Users\\nsdha\\.claude\\plans\\warm-beaming-pretzel.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"9fc54789-06a3-4499-8834-42a3adcc358a","timestamp":"2026-07-03T21:20:40.711Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"update","filePath":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\.claude\\plans\\warm-beaming-pretzel.md","content":"# LONGVIEW graph enrichment — cross-document linking, typed relations, categorisation\n\n## Context\n\nThe Documents graph fix (shipped v1.11.1) made LONGVIEW's real knowledge graph visible, and it\nexposed a deeper problem: **the graph can't show cross-session patterns because there are almost no\ncross-document connections.** Investigation of the live `longview` graph proved the gaps:\n\n| Finding | Evidence |\n|---|---|\n| Every knowledge edge is intra-document | 1,400 / 1,400 RELATES_TO endpoints share a source; **0 cross-document** |\n| Concepts bridge docs only by exact name match | 2,063 of 2,118 concepts are sourced from exactly 1 document; only ~55 shared |\n| Typed relations don't exist as edges | `PREREQUISITE_FOR / CONFLICTS_WITH / ANALOGOUS_TO / CORRELATES_WITH` = **0 in the whole DB**; everything is `RELATES_TO {predicate:<free text>}` |\n| Code↔docs never correlated | `CORRELATES_WITH` = 0 for longview; the 200k-node code graph is fully disjoint from the 2,118 concepts |\n| No categorisation | `concept.category` and `concept.domain` are **null for all 2,118**; embeddings are **not persisted**; `community_id` is set but only clusters within document islands |\n\nRoot cause in code:\n- `save_knowledge_triples()` (`runtime/benny/graph/triples.py`) writes `MERGE (s:Concept {name,workspace})`,\n  one `RELATES_TO {predicate}` per triple, and `SOURCED_FROM`. Relationships only ever connect a\n  triple's subject→object — always the same document. Cross-doc bridging relies entirely on **exact\n  name-MERGE**, which rarely fires (names are verbatim: `\"strategy\" field`, `Vaild JSON Output`).\n- `run_safe_correlation` / `run_aggressive_correlation` (`runtime/benny/synthesis/correlation.py`) link\n  **Concept↔CodeEntity only**, never Concept↔Concept, and were never invoked in the longview path.\n\nSo the answer to \"gap in correlation logic, or need more relations/categorisation?\" is **both**: there\nis no cross-document concept linking at all, relation types are collapsed to one, and concepts carry\nno category/embedding. (Separately, 73,746 `:Concept` nodes named after files — `src`, `CLAUDE.md` — are\nmislabeled **code-structure** nodes wired via `REPRESENTS`→`CodeEntity`; the connected Documents view\nalready excludes them, but they should not share the `:Concept` label.)\n\n**Decisions (from user):** merge near-duplicate concepts **then** add similarity links; **size nodes by\nhow many merges collapsed into them** (recurring-across-sessions concepts grow); **backfill the existing\nlongview graph now AND fix the pipeline** so future runs do it automatically.\n\n## Approach\n\nDeliver a reusable enrichment module invoked both as a one-off backfill (`benny longview enrich-graph\n--workspace longview [--dry-run]`, hung on the existing `benny longview` CLI group) and wired into the\ningest/reduce path for forward runs. Stages run in order; each is idempotent and has a dry-run that\nreports counts without writing. **Take a Neo4j backup / dump before the first non-dry run** (Stages 2 & 4\nmutate/delete).\n\n### Stage 1 — Persist embeddings + categorise\n- Backfill `c.embedding` on all doc concepts by reusing `batch_embed_concepts()` (correlation.py); add a\n  Neo4j vector index so later stages and RAG reuse them instead of recomputing.\n- Assign `c.category` (kg3d palette vocabulary in `runtime/benny/graph/kg3d/` — see `ingest.py`/`ontology.py`/\n  `palette.ts`) + `c.domain` via embedding nearest-centroid or a batched LLM classifier. Enables node\n  colour + theme grouping even where explicit edges are sparse.\n\n### Stage 2 — Canonical merge (dedup) — **the primary bridge builder**\n- Cluster concept embeddings; merge variants above a high cosine (≥0.90) **and** normalized-name match into\n  one canonical node. Repoint `SOURCED_FROM` + `RELATES_TO` to the canonical, delete variants.\n- Set `c.merge_count` = variants collapsed and `c.doc_count` = distinct sources; keep `c.aliases` (merged\n  names) for auditability/reversibility. A concept recurring across sessions now has multi-doc\n  `SOURCED_FROM` automatically → the first real cross-document bridges.\n\n### Stage 3 — Cross-document similarity edges (link)\n- A Concept↔Concept analogue of `run_aggressive_correlation`: for concepts in **different** documents with\n  cosine ≥ 0.82, emit a typed edge `RELATES_TO {predicate:'semantically_similar', strategy:'similarity',\n  confidence:<cos>}` (top-k per concept, ANN via the existing hnswlib path). This is the cross-session web.\n  Reuse `compute_cluster_similarities()` (engine.py) where possible.\n\n### Stage 4 — Typed relation promotion\n- Normalize the free-text `r.predicate` on existing/ new `RELATES_TO` into a controlled vocabulary and set\n  `r.rel_class` ∈ {prerequisite, conflict, analogy, similarity, relates}. Optionally also emit the matching\n  real typed edge (`PREREQUISITE_FOR`…) so kg3d AoT layering (`ontology.py`) and typed pattern queries work.\n  Backfill classifies existing predicates with a cheap map + LLM fallback.\n\n### Stage 5 — Code↔docs correlation\n- Invoke the **existing, unused** `run_full_correlation_suite(workspace='longview')` → `CORRELATES_WITH`\n  edges linking concepts to the 200k code entities (safe exact-match + aggressive embedding ≥0.82).\n\n### Stage 6 — Recluster + surface\n- Re-run `ClusteringService.run_lpa_on_workspace()` now that cross-doc edges exist → communities span\n  documents; `name_community()` labels them.\n- Backend `get_knowledge_graph()` (`runtime/benny/core/graph_db.py`, added in v1.11.1): also return\n  `merge_count`, `category`, `community_id`, `community_name`.\n- Widget `synoptic_web/index.js`: size nodes by `merge_count` (map into the `metrics.pagerank` the layout\n  already uses for radius) and colour by `category`; optional community grouping/legend.\n\n### Pipeline fix (forward)\n- Wire Stages 1–6 after triple persistence in the ingest/longview-reduce orchestration (the caller of\n  `save_knowledge_triples` in `runtime/benny/api/rag_routes.py` and the longview reduce path) so future\n  ingests categorise, merge, cross-link, correlate, and recluster automatically.\n\n### Critical files\n- `runtime/benny/synthesis/correlation.py` — reuse `batch_embed_concepts`; add concept↔concept similarity + canonical-merge functions\n- `runtime/benny/graph/triples.py` — write `rel_class`; carry `merge_count` on write path\n- `runtime/benny/graph/clustering_service.py` — recluster after new edges\n- `runtime/benny/graph/kg3d/{ingest,ontology}.py` + `palette.ts` — category vocabulary/classifier\n- `runtime/benny/synthesis/engine.py` — reuse `compute_cluster_similarities`, `name_community`\n- `runtime/benny/core/graph_db.py` — expose merge_count/category/community in `get_knowledge_graph`\n- `app/L0/_all/mod/_prime_silo/widgets/kg3d/synoptic_web/index.js` — size by merge_count, colour by category\n- new: `runtime/benny/graph/graph_enrichment.py` (orchestrator) + `benny longview enrich-graph` subcommand; wire into `rag_routes.py` ingest\n\n## Verification\n- **Before/after Cypher (nexus `execute_cypher`)**: cross-document RELATES_TO (0 → N); `CORRELATES_WITH`\n  (0 → N); concepts with `category` (0 → 2,118); multi-doc concepts (55 → materially higher);\n  `r.rel_class` distribution non-trivial; community count that spans ≥2 sources.\n- **Dry-run first**: `--dry-run` prints per-stage counts (candidates to merge, edges to add) with zero writes;\n  eyeball before the real run; Neo4j backup taken.\n- **Idempotency**: run the backfill twice → second run adds ~0 (merge/link/correlate all MERGE-guarded).\n- **Widget**: recurring concepts render larger (merge_count → radius); categories coloured; communities\n  visibly bridge documents in the Documents graph.\n- **Tests**: unit tests for merge (edges repointed, variants deleted, merge_count/aliases correct,\n  idempotent), similarity threshold + cross-doc-only filter, predicate→rel_class mapping. Run existing\n  `widgets_kg3d_synoptic_web_test.mjs`; add a `graph_enrichment` backend test asserting Concept↔Concept\n  similarity edges are cross-document and code labels are untouched.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":123,"newStart":1,"newLines":108,"lines":["-# Fix Bridge Documents graph for LONGVIEW — lean knowledge endpoint + view modes","+# LONGVIEW graph enrichment — cross-document linking, typed relations, categorisation"," "," ## Context"," ","-The Bridge **Documents** tab graph is blank/failed for the `longview` workspace, and","-the earlier attempt to fix it by *windowing* (a hard 400-node cap) is undesirable —","-the user wants to see everything, without an arbitrary cutoff, and asked whether a","-**less-intensive fallback** is possible.","+The Documents graph fix (shipped v1.11.1) made LONGVIEW's real knowledge graph visible, and it","+exposed a deeper problem: **the graph can't show cross-session patterns because there are almost no","+cross-document connections.** Investigation of the live `longview` graph proved the gaps:"," ","-Live graph stats for `longview` (via nexus `get_graph_stats`) explain everything:","+| Finding | Evidence |","+|---|---|","+| Every knowledge edge is intra-document | 1,400 / 1,400 RELATES_TO endpoints share a source; **0 cross-document** |","+| Concepts bridge docs only by exact name match | 2,063 of 2,118 concepts are sourced from exactly 1 document; only ~55 shared