a `get_knowledge_graph` case asserting code","-  labels/rels are excluded).","+- **Before/after Cypher (nexus `execute_cypher`)**: cross-document RELATES_TO (0 → N); `CORRELATES_WITH`","+  (0 → N); concepts with `category` (0 → 2,118); multi-doc concepts (55 → materially higher);","+  `r.rel_class` distribution non-trivial; community count that spans ≥2 sources.","+- **Dry-run first**: `--dry-run` prints per-stage counts (candidates to merge, edges to add) with zero writes;","+  eyeball before the real run; Neo4j backup taken.","+- **Idempotency**: run the backfill twice → second run adds ~0 (merge/link/correlate all MERGE-guarded).","+- **Widget**: recurring concepts render larger (merge_count → radius); categories coloured; communities","+  visibly bridge documents in the Documents graph.","+- **Tests**: unit tests for merge (edges repointed, variants deleted, merge_count/aliases correct,","+  idempotent), similarity threshold + cross-doc-only filter, predicate→rel_class mapping. Run existing","+  `widgets_kg3d_synoptic_web_test.mjs`; add a `graph_enrichment` backend test asserting Concept↔Concept","+  similarity edges are cross-document and code labels are untouched."]}],"originalFile":"# Fix Bridge Documents graph for LONGVIEW — lean knowledge endpoint + view modes\n\n## Context\n\nThe Bridge **Documents** tab graph is blank/failed for the `longview` workspace, and\nthe earlier attempt to fix it by *windowing* (a hard 400-node cap) is undesirable —\nthe user wants to see everything, without an arbitrary cutoff, and asked whether a\n**less-intensive fallback** is possible.\n\nLive graph stats for `longview` (via nexus `get_graph_stats`) explain everything:\n\n| Label | Count |  | Rel | Count |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Source (documents) | **61** | | RELATES_TO (concept↔concept) | **1,458** |\n| Concept | **75,864** | | SOURCED_FROM (concept→source) | **2,261** |\n| CodeEntity | 201,960 | | REPRESENTS (code) | 201,960 |\n\nTwo root causes, both confirmed in code:\n\n1. **The fallback pulls the entire dual graph.** The Documents widget's fallback calls\n   `/graph/full?show_all=true`. `get_full_graph()` (`runtime/benny/core/graph_db.py:576`)\n   fetches **unbounded** edges whose `valid_rels` include `REPRESENTS` + all code rels,\n   and nodes `WHERE n:Concept OR n:Source OR n:Document OR n:CodeEntity`. For longview that\n   is ~277k nodes + ~206k edges in one JSON — it hangs/500s. The 400-cap was a band-aid on\n   top of this firehose, not a fix.\n\n2. **The 500 never reaches the fallback.** In the widget (`synoptic_web/index.js:384` `load()`),\n   the `/kg3d/ontology` fallback to `/graph/full` only fires when ontology returns **empty**.\n   When ontology *throws* (it 500s on longview because it computes pagerank/betweenness over\n   75k nodes), the outer `catch` calls `renderError` — so the tab shows \"load failed\", never\n   the fallback.\n\nThe real knowledge graph is small: **61 documents + ~3.7k knowledge edges** touching only a\nfew thousand concepts. The other ~72k concepts are **orphans with zero edges** (isolated dots).\nSo \"see everything meaningful\" is inherently light — no windowing needed — once we stop\ndragging in the 200k-node code graph.\n\n**Decision (from user):** ship two toggleable view modes —\n- **Connected** (default): all documents + every concept that has ≥1 edge; orphans hidden,\n  available via a \"Show orphans\" toggle.\n- **Macro** (documents-only): the 61 Source super-nodes sized by concept count; click a\n  document to expand its concepts on demand.\n\n## Approach\n\n### 1. Backend — a lean, code-free knowledge endpoint\n\n`runtime/benny/core/graph_db.py` — add `get_knowledge_graph(workspace, mode, run_id=None, source_id=None)`\n(sibling to `get_full_graph`, reusing its record-shaping helpers). It never touches CodeEntity/REPRESENTS.\n\n- **Knowledge rels only:** `RELATES_TO, SOURCED_FROM, PREREQUISITE_FOR, CONFLICTS_WITH, ANALOGOUS_TO`\n  (drop `REPRESENTS, CODE_REL, DEFINES, CALLS, INHERITS, DEPENDS_ON, CONTAINS, CORRELATES_WITH`).\n- **Knowledge nodes only:** `WHERE n:Concept OR n:Source OR n:Document` (never `CodeEntity`).\n- `mode=\"connected\"` (default): nodes = (all `Source`) ∪ (endpoints of the knowledge edges).\n  Returns ~a few thousand nodes + ~3.7k edges for longview. No cap, no metrics compute.\n- `mode=\"all\"`: connected set **plus** orphan `Concept` nodes (the ~72k dust), edges unchanged.\n- `mode=\"macro\"`: return the 61 `Source` nodes only, each carrying `concept_count`\n  (`SIZE((s)<-[:SOURCED_FROM]-())`), plus `RELATES_TO`-derived co-citation edges between\n  sources if cheap, else no edges. Cheap aggregate Cypher, no per-concept payload.\n- `source_id` (for macro expand-on-click): return one Source + its `SOURCED_FROM` concepts\n  + their `RELATES_TO` edges.\n\n`runtime/benny/api/graph_routes.py` — add `GET /graph/knowledge`\n(params `workspace`, `mode=connected|all|macro`, `source_id?`, `run_id?`) delegating to the new\nfunction. Same `Neo4j not available → 503` / `Exception → 500` guard as `/graph/full` (line 404).\nKeep the existing `/graph/full` untouched (code graph / other callers still use it).\n\n### 2. Frontend widget — trigger the fallback on error, use the lean endpoint, drop the cap\n\n`app/L0/_all/mod/_prime_silo/widgets/kg3d/synoptic_web/index.js`:\n\n- **Fix the trigger (core bug):** in `load()`, wrap the `/kg3d/ontology` call so that a **throw\n  or non-OK** *also* falls through to the fallback (today only an empty payload does). Ontology\n  stays the fast path for small workspaces; longview's 500 now degrades gracefully instead of\n  erroring out.\n- **Repoint + rewrite `loadGraphFullFallback()` → `loadKnowledgeGraph()`:** call\n  `/graph/knowledge?workspace=…&mode=<mode>` instead of `/graph/full?show_all=true`. Keep the\n  same node-shape adaptation (id/display_name/category/aot_layer/metrics) and the\n  connectivity-based layering already there (`Source`→layer 1, hubs high, leaves low).\n- **Remove `FALLBACK_NODE_BUDGET = 400`** and the degree-sort truncation for connected/macro\n  modes (the set is already small). Retain a large safety ceiling **only** for `mode=\"all\"`\n  orphan dust (e.g. 20k) to protect the SVG default renderer used in tests.\n- Add a `mode` prop (`connected` default) and a `sourceId` prop; changing either re-fetches\n  (extend the `fetchKeyChanged` check in `update()`).\n\n### 3. Frontend Bridge — the toggles + a lite render mode\n\n`app/L0/_all/mod/_prime_silo/bridge/bridge.js` (Documents view, `mountKnowledgeGraph()` ~L880):\n\n- State: `docsGraphMode` (`connected|all|macro`), pass as `mode` prop to `createSynopticWebWidget`.\n- Toolbar controls near the existing 3D/physics toggles (~L901): a mode selector\n  **Connected / Everything / Documents**, and in macro mode, clicking a Source calls\n  `mountKnowledgeGraph({ mode:\"connected\", sourceId })` to expand that document.\n- **Less-intensive render (the \"fallback\" the user asked about):** in\n  `makeForceRenderer()` (~L1480) / `force_graph_2d/index.js`, add a **lite profile** that kicks\n  in when node count exceeds a threshold (~2,000): pinned/static layout (no live d3 sim),\n  points-only (labels on hover/zoom/selection instead of always), no `linkDirectionalParticles`,\n  reduced `warmupTicks`/`cooldownTime`. Connected mode rarely trips it; \"Everything\" (orphans)\n  relies on it to stay smooth.\n\n### Critical files\n- `runtime/benny/core/graph_db.py` — new `get_knowledge_graph()` (near `get_full_graph:576`)\n- `runtime/benny/api/graph_routes.py` — new `GET /graph/knowledge` (near `/graph/full:404`)\n- `app/L0/_all/mod/_prime_silo/widgets/kg3d/synoptic_web/index.js` — fallback trigger + endpoint + cap\n- `app/L0/_all/mod/_prime_silo/widgets/force_graph_2d/index.js` — lite render profile\n- `app/L0/_all/mod/_prime_silo/bridge/bridge.js` — mode toggles + expand-on-click\n\n## Verification\n\n- **Backend, direct:** with the runtime up, `GET /graph/knowledge?workspace=longview&mode=connected`\n  returns a few-thousand-node payload in well under a second, with 61 Sources present and **zero**\n  `CodeEntity`/`REPRESENTS`. `mode=macro` returns 61 nodes with `concept_count`. `mode=all` returns\n  ~76k nodes. Compare timing against the old `/graph/full?show_all=true` (expected: hang/500).\n- **Nexus cross-check:** `get_graph_stats(workspace=\"longview\")` Source=61 matches the node count\n  the macro view shows.\n- **Widget unit tests:** extend `tests/widgets_kg3d_synoptic_web_test.mjs` — (a) ontology throw →\n  falls back to `/graph/knowledge` (regression for the core bug); (b) connected payload renders all\n  nodes with no 400 truncation; (c) `mode` prop change refetches.\n- **In-app (Preview/manual):** open Bridge → Documents on longview. Connected mode shows the 61\n  documents + connected concepts fully. Toggle **Everything** → orphans appear and the lite renderer\n  keeps it responsive. Toggle **Documents** → 61 super-nodes; click one → expands to its concepts.\n- **Backend tests:** `pytest runtime/tests/api/ -q` (add a `get_knowledge_graph` case asserting code\n  labels/rels are excluded).\n","userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"093e12e1-8fca-4550-8f49-d9e1799391a8","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16","sessionId":"4cd9df3b-c431-4ac3-8790-b888629655bb","version":"2.1.197","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"warm-beaming-pretzel"}
