, after the Documents-graph fix ([[prime_silo_documents_graph_longview_fix]]) made LONGVIEW's real knowledge graph visible, diagnosed WHY it shows no cross-session patterns and built the fix. See [[project_longview_session_synthesis]].\n\n**Diagnosis (live `longview` graph via nexus execute_cypher):**\n- Every RELATES_TO edge is **intra-document** (1,400/1,400 endpoints share a source; 0 cross-doc). Concepts bridge docs ONLY by exact name-MERGE (`triples.py save_knowledge_triples` does `MERGE (s:Concept {name,workspace})`), so **2,063 of 2,118 concepts are single-document**.\n- **Relations collapsed to one type:** every edge is `RELATES_TO {predicate:<free text>}`; PREREQUISITE_FOR/CONFLICTS_WITH/ANALOGOUS_TO/CORRELATES_WITH = **0 in the whole DB**. But the types are latent — a rel_class dry-run classified longview's 1,458 edges as **43 prerequisite / 35 composition / 1 conflict / 1379 relates**.\n- **Correlation never ran for longview:** 0 CORRELATES_WITH. `synthesis/correlation.py` (run_safe/run_aggressive/run_full_correlation_suite) only links Concept↔**CodeEntity** (never Concept↔Concept), and longview's Node runner bypassed the rag_routes ingest path that calls it.\n- **No categorisation:** concept.category/domain/embedding all null; community_id set (LPA) but only clusters within islands.\n- The \"73k orphans\" = **code-structure nodes mislabeled `:Concept`** (node_type='Concept', REPRESENTS→CodeEntity, named after files: `src`, `CLAUDE.md`). The connected Documents view already excludes them (they have no SOURCED_FROM).\n\n**Fix — new `runtime/benny/graph/graph_enrichment.py` + `benny enrich-graph --workspace W [--apply] [--stages ...]` CLI** (commit b2ecb34, on main). Dry-run by default. Six idempotent stages: (1) persist c.embedding via `batch_embed_concepts` (from synthesis.engine, provider='local'→lemonade); (2) **canonical merge** near-dups (cosine≥0.90 + name Jaccard≥0.5, union-find, canonical=most-sources), repoint SOURCED_FROM+RELATES_TO, set `merge_count`/`aliases`/`doc_count`; (3) **cross-doc similarity** RELATES_TO{predicate:'semantically_similar'} cosine≥0.82 cross-doc only; (4) `rel_class` from predicate; (5) run_full_correlation_suite (code↔docs); (6) recluster LPA + category=community_name. Merge Cypher uses `CALL {}` unit subqueries (no APOC — apoc.coll.toSet is absent).\n- **Surfacing:** `graph_db.py get_knowledge_graph()` now returns merge_count/category/community_id/community_name; widget `synoptic_web/index.js` sizes nodes by merge_count (recurring-across-sessions concepts grow) and colours by theme (new `hashCategoryColor` gives community names stable distinct HSL, since they aren't in the academic CATEGORY_COLORS palette).\n- **Pipeline (forward):** `rag_routes.py` ingest runs additive stages (embeddings/similarity/rel_class) automatically after synthesis, BEFORE the existing LPA+correlation block; destructive merge is opt-in via `IngestRequest.enrich_merge` (default False).\n\n**Verified:** rel_class live dry-run; merge + similarity write Cypher pass EXPLAIN on live Neo4j; 5 pytest unit tests (classify_predicate/normalize/jaccard/union_find) in `runtime/tests/graph/test_graph_enrichment.py`; widget mjs tests green; all py_compile.\n\n**BLOCKED / not done:** the embed→merge→similarity backfill's live merge-count is unverified — **lemonade embedding endpoint (:13305) wedges under the 2,118-concept load** (works in ~120-concept bursts at 172ms/concept ≈ 6min for 2,118, but drops connections mid-run: \"Failed to connect to lemonade embedding endpoint\"). Matches the known lemonade generation wedge. To finish: with lemonade stable, `benny enrich-graph --workspace longview --stages embeddings,merge` (dry-run) → eyeball merge count → **Neo4j backup** → `--apply` (merge DELETES variant nodes). Not tagged/released yet (v1.11.1 was the prior Documents-graph fix).\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":22,"oldLines":4,"newStart":22,"newLines":12,"lines":[" "," **Verified:** rel_class live dry-run; merge + similar