ncept↔**CodeEntity** (never Concept↔Concept), and longview's Node runner bypassed the rag_routes ingest path that calls it.\n- **No categorisation:** concept.category/domain/embedding all null; community_id set (LPA) but only clusters within islands.\n- The \"73k orphans\" = **code-structure nodes mislabeled `:Concept`** (node_type='Concept', REPRESENTS→CodeEntity, named after files: `src`, `CLAUDE.md`). The connected Documents view already excludes them (they have no SOURCED_FROM).\n\n**Fix — new `runtime/benny/graph/graph_enrichment.py` + `benny enrich-graph --workspace W [--apply] [--stages ...]` CLI** (commit b2ecb34, on main). Dry-run by default. Six idempotent stages: (1) persist c.embedding via `batch_embed_concepts` (from synthesis.engine, provider='local'→lemonade); (2) **canonical merge** near-dups (cosine≥0.90 + name Jaccard≥0.5, union-find, canonical=most-sources), repoint SOURCED_FROM+RELATES_TO, set `merge_count`/`aliases`/`doc_count`; (3) **cross-doc similarity** RELATES_TO{predicate:'semantically_similar'} cosine≥0.82 cross-doc only; (4) `rel_class` from predicate; (5) run_full_correlation_suite (code↔docs); (6) recluster LPA + category=community_name. Merge Cypher uses `CALL {}` unit subqueries (no APOC — apoc.coll.toSet is absent).\n- **Surfacing:** `graph_db.py get_knowledge_graph()` now returns merge_count/category/community_id/community_name; widget `synoptic_web/index.js` sizes nodes by merge_count (recurring-across-sessions concepts grow) and colours by theme (new `hashCategoryColor` gives community names stable distinct HSL, since they aren't in the academic CATEGORY_COLORS palette).\n- **Pipeline (forward):** `rag_routes.py` ingest runs additive stages (embeddings/similarity/rel_class) automatically after synthesis, BEFORE the existing LPA+correlation block; destructive merge is opt-in via `IngestRequest.enrich_merge` (default False).\n\n**Verified:** rel_class live dry-run; merge + similarity write Cypher pass EXPLAIN on live Neo4j; 5 pytest unit tests (classify_predicate/normalize/jaccard/union_find) in `runtime/tests/graph/test_graph_enrichment.py`; widget mjs tests green; all py_compile.\n\n**EXECUTED LIVE on longview (2026-07-03, released v1.11.2/v1.11.3):**\n- rel_class applied: 43 prerequisite / 35 composition / 1 conflict / 1379 relates.\n- embeddings: 2,118 persisted (lemonade `nomic-embed-text-v1-GGUF`, flaky — wedges under load but pushed through on retry).\n- similarity: **563 cross-document links (0→563, all genuinely cross-doc)** — the case-variant recurrence is the story (\"Maintenance Task\" vs \"Maintenance task\" across 4 docs; name-MERGE in triples.py is case-SENSITIVE, which is why 2,063/2,118 were single-doc).\n- recluster: **48 of 60 themes named / 577 concepts categorized** (timeout clipped the 12 smallest). qwen3.5 themes are good: \"L2 Expertise & Architecture\" (48), \"Prime-Silo Architecture Suite\" (34), \"Full-Stack DevOps Pipeline\", \"Runtime Failure Diagnostics\", \"CSS Variable Migration\", \"Pype Data Lineage\", \"Agent Memory & Paranoia\"…\n\n**MODEL CORRECTION (important):** `qwen3.5-9b-FLM` is a **lemonade** model (`MODEL_REGISTRY.local_lemonade`, provider=lemonade), NOT fastflowlm (fastflowlm's model is `openai/deepseek-r1:8b`). The \"DeepSeek\" I first saw was the router auto-detect fallback (`_get_active_model_raw` step 4 probes LOCAL_PROVIDERS, returns first responder = lemonade's loaded model) because no BENNY_DEFAULT_MODEL/manifest default_model is set. Added `benny enrich-graph --model lemonade/qwen3.5-9b-FLM` (sets BENNY_DEFAULT_MODEL, router priority -1; commit 65d9773). FLM thinking-suppression is automatic (fragile models). Also fixed recluster LPA scope: was `ClusteringService.run_lpa_on_workspace` (whole 277k-node graph → hung); now a self-contained LPA over just the ~2k knowledge nodes, MIN_NAMED_COMMUNITY=4/MAX_NAMED_COMMUNITIES=60 (commit 1075cd1). Released **v1.11.3**.\n\n**STILL HELD — canonical merge (destructive).** `--stages merge --apply` NOT run — it DELETES variant nodes. The 563 similarity links show the merge targets clearly (case/punctuation variants at cosine≥0.97). To do: **Neo4j backup** → `benny enrich-graph --workspace longview --stages merge --apply` → merge_count then drives node size in the widget. Also: forward pipeline runs additive stages auto (rag_routes), merge opt-in via IngestRequest.enrich_merge.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":30,"oldLines":4,"newStart":30,"newLines":10,"lines":[" "," **MODEL CORRECTION (important):** `qwen3.5-9b-FLM` is a **lemonade** model (`MODEL_REGISTRY.local_lemonade`, provider=lemonade), NOT fastflowlm (fastflowlm's model is `openai/deepseek-r1:8b`). The \"DeepSeek\" I first saw was the router auto-detect fallback (`_get_active_model_raw` step 4 probes LOCAL_PROVIDERS, returns first responder = lemonade's loaded model) because no BENNY_DEFAULT_MODEL/manifest default_model is set. Added `benny enrich-graph --model lemonade/qwen3.5-9b-FLM` (sets BENNY_DEFAULT_MODEL, router priority -1; commit 65d9773). FLM thinking-suppression is automatic (fragile models). Also fixed recluster LPA scope: was `ClusteringService.run_lpa_on_workspace` (whole 277k-node graph → hung); now a self-contained LPA over just the ~2k knowledge nodes, MIN_NAMED_COMMUNITY=4/MAX_NAMED_COMMUNITIES=60 (commit 1075cd1). Released **v1.11.3**."," ","-**STILL HELD — canonical merge (destructive).** `--stages merge --apply` NOT run — it DELETES variant nodes. The 563 similarity links show the merge targets clearly (case/punctuation variants at cosine≥0.97). To do: **Neo4j backup** → `benny enrich-graph --workspace longview --stages merge --apply` → merge_count then drives node size in the widget. Also: forward pipeline runs additive stages auto (rag_routes), merge opt-in via IngestRequest.enrich_merge.","+**RECLUSTER TAIL + CANONICAL MERGE — DONE (2026-07-04).** Recluster completed all **60 themes / 649 concepts** categorized (was 48/577; a Neo4j :7687 crash mid-run had blocked it — user relaunche