{"parentUuid":"36e70987-a64f-411d-81f8-0354e2b7f735","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"5e087aad-4ca6-455b-83d4-dbdbc651cd2a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GwHV8UEMJQsvZztMwU6kWW","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# LONGVIEW — run & test guide\n2\t\n3\tTurns months of local agent sessions (Antigravity brain + Claude Code, via the\n4\tmemo-ray entity store) into a workspace knowledge graph and cited deliverables —\n5\tportfolio report, PRD, operator skill, project dossiers, book, TOGAF prep — all\n6\ton the local model, for electricity instead of tokens.\n7\t\n8\t- Design: [`architecture/ADR-005-longview-session-synthesis.md`](../../architecture/ADR-005-longview-session-synthesis.md)\n9\t- Definition of record: [`manifests/templates/longview_synthesis.json`](../../manifests/templates/longview_synthesis.json)\n10\t- Runner internals: [`scripts/longview/README.md`](../../../scripts/longview/README.md)\n11\t\n12\t## Prerequisites\n13\t\n14\t| What | Check |\n15\t| ---- | ----- |\n16\t| Lemonade on `:13305` with `qwen3.5-9b-FLM` | `curl http://127.0.0.1:13305/api/v1/models` |\n17\t| Benny runtime on `:8005` | `curl -H \"X-Benny-API-Key: benny-mesh-2026-auth\" http://127.0.0.1:8005/api/offload/health` |\n18\t| memo-ray checkout sibling of prime-silo | its server running is optional (sync falls back to direct parsers) |\n19\t| Node.js on PATH | the runner is Node; `benny longview` shells out to it |\n20\t\n21\tThe workspace lives under the **runtime's resolved home** (desktop config →\n22\te.g. `%APPDATA%\\space-agent\\benny-home\\benny\\workspaces\\longview`), never the\n23\trepo. The runner resolves it identically via `packaging/desktop/home_resolver.js`.\n24\t\n25\t## Run from the EXE (v1.9.1+)\n26\t\n27\tNo terminal needed — both surfaces call the same launcher and read the same\n28\tdisk-truth status (runner lock + heartbeat), so runs started anywhere show\n29\teverywhere:\n30\t\n31\t- **Tray** — right-click Prime-Silo: `LONGVIEW: idle/running (…)` status line,\n32\t  **Run LONGVIEW delta sync**, **Stop LONGVIEW (resume-safe)**, and\n33\t  **Open LONGVIEW outputs**.\n34\t- **Bridge → Documents** (workspace `longview`) — the **LONGVIEW pipeline**\n35\t  panel: *Run delta sync* / *Run full pipeline* / *Stop*, with a live heartbeat\n36\t  (phase, cards done/total, failures, ETA) and the last runner log line while\n37\t  running. Deliverables appear below in **Outputs**.\n38\t- **API** — `POST /api/longview_run {\"mode\":\"delta\"|\"all\"|\"<phase>\"}`,\n39\t  `GET /api/longview_status`, `POST /api/longview_stop`.\n40\t\n41\tThe child process logs to `<workspace>/longview/runner.log`; only one runner\n42\tper workspace can hold the lock, regardless of launcher.\n43\t\n44\t## Commands (all from `prime-silo/runtime/`)\n45\t\n46\t```powershell\n47\tpython benny_cli.py longview run                  # all enabled phases, resume-safe\n48\tpython benny_cli.py longview run --phase map      # one phase (also retries failed cards)\n49\tpython benny_cli.py longview run --delta          # only new/changed sessions\n50\tpython benny_cli.py longview status               # heartbeat: phase, counts, ETA\n51\tpython benny_cli.py longview report               # honest ledger report\n52\t```\n53\t\n54\tPhases (declared in the manifest, executed in order):\n55\t`inventory` → `extract` → `map` → `model` → `code` → `weave` → `reduce` → `opus` → `pdf`.\n56\tEdit the manifest to change model, budgets, batch sizes, `deep_synthesis`,\n57\tloop counts, or to disable phases — no code changes.\n58\t\n59\t**Phase isolation (v1.10.1):** a phase that throws is ledgered as a\n60\t`phase_error` entry and skipped — the remaining phases still run. (Before this,\n61\tan opus outline parse failure killed the whole process and took the pdf phase\n62\twith it.) Check `longview report` / the ledger after a full run; a missing\n63\tdeliverable now always has a ledger entry saying why.\n64\t\n65\t- **code** — junctions the repo into `<workspace>/src/` and runs `benny enrich`\n66\t  (Tree-Sitter scan → code graph → `CORRELATES_WITH` links to the knowledge\n67\t  concepts). The dual graph is what lets later phases cross-reference decisions\n68\t  to the code they shaped.\n69\t- **weave** — discovery loops (`weave_loops` × `weave_questions`): the model\n70\t  proposes under-explored questions, each is answered from retrieval (vector\n71\t  chunks + graph concepts) into a **cited discovery note**, and the notes are\n72\t  ingested back — so every loop, and every deliverable after it, stands on a\n73\t  richer corpus. This is the compounding \"greater than the sum\" mechanism.\n74\t- **opus** — *The AI Vampire*: a 200+ page narrative-nonfiction book built\n75\t  hierarchically (one outline call → per-chapter section specs → ~100\n76\t  retrieval-grounded sections of 650–950 words, each cited, each resume-safe\n77\t  as a file under `data_out/opus/sections/`). Assembles to\n78\t  `data_out/opus/THE-AI-VAMPIRE.md`; partial assemblies are valid previews.\n79\t- **pdf** — the assembled book → print-styled HTML → PDF via headless\n80\t  Edge/Chrome: `data_out/opus/THE-AI-VAMPIRE.pdf`.\n81\t\n82\t## Book on demand (decoupled from ingestion)\n83\t\n84\tThe book does **not** need the model/ingest phase: the opus phase reads\n85\tTHEMES.md + dossiers from `data_out/` and pulls evidence by retrieval from the\n86\tvectors and graph that already exist. Once a corpus is in place, regenerate the\n87\tbook (and nothing else) with:\n88\t\n89\t```powershell\n90\tnode scripts/longview/longview.mjs reduce --only dossiers,themes,report   # refresh the foundation (~30-40 min)\n91\tnode scripts/longview/longview.mjs opus                                   # ~100 sections, resume-safe per section\n92\tnode scripts/longview/longview.mjs pdf                                    # THE-AI-VAMPIRE.pdf via headless Edge\n93\t```\n94\t\n95\tSkip the first command if the foundation is current. Operational rule: **never\n96\trun a de