\n78\tWrites `build/THE-AI-VAMPIRE.wav` (chapters concatenated in manifest order with\n79\tsilence gaps) and `build/chapters.cue.txt` (start timestamp per chapter). All\n80\tchapter WAVs must share one format (channels/width/rate) — they will, coming from\n81\tone profile+engine; a mismatch is reported instead of silently corrupting output.\n82\t\n83\t### Optional: WAV → MP3 / M4B\n84\t\n85\tThe deliverable is a WAV so the pipeline stays dependency-free. To compress or\n86\tmake a chaptered `.m4b`, install ffmpeg and, e.g.:\n87\t\n88\t```\n89\tffmpeg -i build/THE-AI-VAMPIRE.wav -b:a 128k build/THE-AI-VAMPIRE.mp3\n90\t```\n91\t\n92\t(The cue sheet has the chapter offsets for building m4b chapter metadata.)\n93\t\n94\t## Determinism guarantees\n95\t\n96\t- Chapter order = numeric sort of section filenames → identical every run.\n97\t- Fixed output names (`chNN.txt`, `chNN.wav`) → re-runs overwrite, never reorder.\n98\t- Stitch order = `manifest.json` order, not directory listing order.\n99\t- No timestamps or randomness enter the text or the assembly.\n100\t"}]},"uuid":"c388a6eb-25e9-4704-ae4d-8ced83ac1319","timestamp":"2026-07-04T08:25:34.200Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"prime-silo\\scripts\\longview\\audiobook\\README.md","content":"# The AI Vampire — Audiobook Workflow (Prime-Silo)\n\nDeterministic pipeline that turns `data_out/opus/THE-AI-VAMPIRE.md` into a single\nnarrated audiobook WAV, one chapter at a time, via **Voicebox** (local TTS,\n`voicebox.sh`) and stitches the chapters back together in fixed order.\n\n```\n01_prepare.py     markdown  ->  clean, '#'-free per-chapter text + manifest.json\n02_synthesize.py  driver/tracker for the Voicebox MCP step (the TTS itself)\n03_stitch.py      per-chapter WAVs  ->  one audiobook WAV + chapter cue sheet\nbuild/            all generated artifacts live here\n```\n\nEverything except the actual speech synthesis is pure Python stdlib — no ffmpeg,\nno third-party packages. Ordering is derived only 