{"parentUuid":"9ce868c3-30bf-4855-af98-b11c8de3b2c4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_0184J64e4j3wfVHpevWmqsKi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The re-run with the repair fix proves your point exactly. It went from ok=1/fail=4 to **ok=4/fail=1** — but look at the one that still failed:\n\n```\nFAIL b708c23f — decisions: array of strings required; outcomes: array of strings required; failures: array of strings required\n```\n\nThat card got **truncated before it even produced its decisions/outcomes/failures** — the repair salvaged a syntactically-valid object, but the substance was gone, so the gate correctly rejected it. That's your concern made concrete: **repair keeps the JSON parseable, not the knowledge.** Cramming a whole session into one call is the root problem — both on input (evidence capped at 7,500 chars) and output (card truncates at ~450 tokens).\n\n## Your proposal is the correct architecture\n\nWhat you're describing is a **hierarchical, graph-walked map-reduce** where every context stays short and nothing is distilled from truncated text:\n\n1. **Walk the session's timeline graph.** memo-ray already stores each session as a graph of step entities (User Input → Thought → Tool Call → Tool Result → Artifact) linked by `children_ids` — `store.mjs readTimeline(sessionId)` already returns them in order. Today `evidence.mjs` flattens+truncates that into one 7,500-char blob; instead we walk it.\n2. **Extract per short window.** Chunk the walk into small windows (a few steps / ~1–1.5k chars). Each extraction call has a tiny context → no input loss, no output truncation, full fidelity. Out comes a small structured slice: concepts, decisions, artifacts, citations for *that* window.\n3. **Roll up losslessly.** Aggregate the window slices into the session card. The rollup's input is the already-distilled structured slices (short), not the raw session — so it never truncates either.\n4. **Then the \"greater than the sum\" pass.** Once concepts + relations exist in the graph, a review pass walks the *concept* graph across sessions to synthesize what no single session showed. This is exactly what the `weave` phase (discovery loops) and my new `enrich` phase (merge / cross-doc links / themes) already begin — your idea makes the *extraction itself* graph-native so that review stands on complete, not truncated, concepts.\n\n**Net:** map becomes map-over-steps (short) + reduce-over-slices (short), instead of one-shot-over-a-session (long, lossy). Trade-off is more LLM calls per session — but each is short and fast on the 9B model, and crucially **lossless**. `repairTruncatedJson` drops back to being a rare safety net, not the normal path.\n\nThis is a real redesign of the `map`/`extract` phases, and it directly serves the v2 goal. I'd want to plan it properly (chunking boundaries, the per-window extraction schema, the rollup/merge contract, resume-safety per window) rather than bolt it on. Let me put together a concrete plan."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3774,"cache_read_input_tokens":565896,"output_tokens":2700,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3774,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2700,"cache_read_input_tokens":565896,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3774,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3774},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CcgkXT6bD1dSr2jigqZzG","type":"assistant","uuid":"199d2610-d4ec-4923-9a6d-4f9f0602374f","timestamp":"2026-07-04T09:06:42.555Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16","sessionId":"4cd9df3b-c431-4ac3-8790-b888629655bb","ver