 failing `b708c23f`; assert the cards have populated `decisions/outcomes/failures` (no empty lists\n  from lossy repair).\n- **Fidelity spot-check**: compare a graph-walk card vs the old single-call card for one large session\n  — fuller lists, citations intact.\n- **Resume**: interrupt map mid-session, rerun → cached windows are skipped (queue shrinks by completed\n  windows, not whole sessions).\n- **Review**: `review` phase writes `data_out/reviews/*.md` citing graph concepts + cross-session links.\n- **End to end**: full `longview run` on `longview_v2` completes through `pdf`; then the book + Kokoro\n  audiobook per the prior plan.\n\n## Sequencing\nBuild + pilot this **before** the full v2 run, so the whole corpus is extracted losslessly. The\n`enrich` phase (committed `47b6f11`) and the memo-ray source fix (`6e56b9c` + `.env`) stay as-is; this\nreplaces only the extraction path (`map`) and adds `review`.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":96,"newStart":1,"newLines":89,"lines":["-# LONGVIEW v2 — clean end-to-end run in a fresh workspace (enrichment + book + audiobook)","+# LONGVIEW graph-walk extraction — lossless cards + post-graph session review"," "," ## Context"," ","-The Documents-graph fix and the cross-document enrichment (merge / similarity / typed relations /","-themes) all shipped this session (v1.11.1–v1.11.4) and were validated by **backfilling the existing","-`longview` graph in place**. We now want a **clean, end-to-end validation on the latest release**:","-re-run the whole LONGVIEW pipeline over all sessions in a **fresh workspace**, with the enrichment","-built into the pipeline, producing *The AI Vampire* v2 **and** its audiobook — proving the full","-flow (sessions → graph → enrichment → book → PDF → narrated WAV) works from nothing on v1.11.4.","+The v2 map pilot exposed a hard limit: qwen3.5-9b-FLM **self-limits its output to ~415 tokens","+regardless of `max_tokens`** — proven by diagnostic (`finish_reason=\"stop\"`, not `\"len