step covered exactly once) and window order is deterministic across two runs; each window ≤ budget.","+- **Pilot**: `LONGVIEW_WORKSPACE=longview_v2 map --limit 5` → **ok=5/5**, including the previously","+  failing `b708c23f`; assert the cards have populated `decisions/outcomes/failures` (no empty lists","+  from lossy repair).","+- **Fidelity spot-check**: compare a graph-walk card vs the old single-call card for one large session","+  — fuller lists, citations intact.","+- **Resume**: interrupt map mid-session, rerun → cached windows are skipped (queue shrinks by completed","+  windows, not whole sessions).","+- **Review**: `review` phase writes `data_out/reviews/*.md` citing graph concepts + cross-session links.","+- **End to end**: full `longview run` on `longview_v2` completes through `pdf`; then the book + Kokoro","+  audiobook per the prior plan."," ","-## Risks / guardrails","-- **Never run a deep-synthesis ingest concurrently with reduce/opus** (Lemonade wedge → 0-byte","-  deliverables) — the single sequential `longview run` respects this.","-- Lemonade/Neo4j stability (both wedged/crashed earlier) — phase isolation + resume make restarts","-  cheap; monitor `longview status`.","-- Full backlog is long (guide reference ~52 cards/hr map + per-doc synthesis) — the pilot slice","-  (step 2) proves the model/gate before committing the hours.","+## Sequencing","+Build + pilot this **before** the full v2 run, so the whole corpus is extracted losslessly. The","+`enrich` phase (committed `47b6f11`) and the memo-ray source fix (`6e56b9c` + `.env`) stay as-is; this","+replaces only the extraction path (`map`) and adds `review`."]}],"originalFile":"# LONGVIEW v2 — clean end-to-end run in a fresh workspace (enrichment + book + audiobook)\n\n## Context\n\nThe Documents-graph fix and the cross-document enrichment (merge / similarity / typed relations /\nthemes) all shipped this session (v1.11.1–v1.11.4) and were validated by **backfilling the existing\n`longview` graph in place**. We now want a **clean, end-to-end validation on the latest release**:\nre-run the whole LONGVIEW pipeline over all sessions in a **fresh workspace**, with the enrichment\nbuilt into the pipeline, producing *The AI Vampire* v2 **and** its audiobook — proving the full\nflow (sessions → graph → enrichment → book → PDF → narrated WAV) works from nothing on v1.11.4.\n\nA fresh workspace (`longview_v2`) keeps the already-enriched `longview` graph untouched and gives a\ntrue baseline. The runner already parameterises the workspace via `LONGVIEW_WORKSPACE`\n(`scripts/longview/lib/config.mjs:51`), so nothing is hard-coded to `longview`.\n\n**Decisions (user):** wire enrichment as a real pipeline **phase** (one-command E2E, repeatable);\naudiobook narrated with **Kokoro (bf_emma)** via `02_run_kokoro.py`.\n\n## Approach\n\n### 1. Wire an `enrich` phase into the runner (small code change)\n`scripts/longview/longview.mjs` — add `runEnrichGraph()` mirroring the existing `runCode()`\n(~line 764, which shells `benny_cli.py enrich … --run` and ledgers). It shells:\n`python benny_cli.py enrich-graph --workspace <config.WORKSPACE> --apply --model lemonade/qwen3.5-9b-FLM`,\nstrips the braille-spinner glyphs like `runCode` does, and writes a `phase: \"enrich\"` ledger +\n`writeStatus({phase:\"enrich\"})`. Register it in the phase dispatch next to `code`.\n\n`runtime/manifests/templates/longview_synthesis.json` — add `{ \"id\": \"enrich\", \"enabled\": true }`\n**after `weave`, before `reduce`** (graph is populated by `model`; `weave` has ingested discovery\nnotes; enrichment then connects/merges/themes the whole corpus before the deliverables read it).\nFinal order: `inventory → extract → map → model → code → weave → enrich → reduce → opus → pdf`.\n\nNote: on a full run the `enrich` phase runs all stages incl. **canonical merge** (safe/idempotent —\nonly collapses near-identical dups; a fresh workspace has nothing precious). Delta runs re-run the\nadditive stages naturally. Reuses the persisted-embedding fast path (v1.11.4).\n\n### 2. Bootstrap the clean workspace + pilot (de-risk before the multi-hour run)\nSet `LONGVIEW_WORKSPACE=longview_v2` for every command. Follow the guide's test procedure\n(`runtime/docs/operations/LONGVIEW_GUIDE.md` §Test procedure):\n- `longview inventory` → `extract` → `map --limit 5` → `longview report` (expect cards ok > 0).\n- Prove resume (Ctrl-C mid-map, rerun → queue shrinks by ledgered sessions).\n\n### 3. Full pipeline run (all sessions)\n`LONGVIEW_WORKSPACE=longview_v2 python benny_cli.py longview run` (resume-safe; walk away — hours).\nEquivalent via the app: tray **Run LONGVIEW** or Bridge → Documents (workspace `longview_v2`) →\n**Run full pipeline**. Phase isolation (v1.10.1) means any throwing phase is ledgered `phase_error`\nand skipped, never fatal.\n\n### 4. Book verification\n`workspaces/longview_v2/data_out/opus/THE-AI-VAMPIRE.md` (assembled, ~72 sections) + `.pdf`.\nIf `opus`/`pdf` shows a `phase_error`: rerun `longview run --phase opus` then `--phase pdf`\n(both resume-safe per-section).\n\n### 5. Audiobook (Kokoro)\nVoicebox running (backend `:17493`). Point the pipeline at the v2 book and run the 3 stages from\n`scripts/longview/audiobook/`:\n- `LONGVIEW_BOOK_DIR=<home>/workspaces/longview_v2/data_out/opus python 01_prepare.py`\n  (`01_prepare.py:39` honours `LONGVIEW_BOOK_DIR`) → `build/chapters/chNN.txt` + `manifest.json`.\n- `python 02_run_kokoro.py` (Kokoro `bf_emma`, `POST /generate`, resume-safe per chapter) →\n  `build/audio/chNN.wav`.\n- `python 03_stitch.py` → `build/THE-AI-VAMPIRE.wav` + `build/chapters.cue.txt`.\n- Optional: ffmpeg WAV → MP3/M4B.\n\n### Critical files\n- `scripts/longview/longview.mjs` — new `runEnrichGraph()` + dispatch (mirror `runCode`)\n- `runtime/manifests/templates/longview_synthesis.json` — add the `enrich` phase\n- (audiobook scripts + `enrich-graph` CLI already exist — no change)\n\n## Prerequisites (verify first)\n- v1.11.4 installed; runtime `:8005` up (`/api/offload/health`); **Neo4j up** (it and Lemonade both\n  dropped earlier this session — the app supervises them).\n- Lemonade `:13305` serving `qwen3.5-9b-FLM` (+ `nomic-embed-text-v1-GGUF` for embeddings).\n- memo-ray reachable (session source; sync falls back to direct parsers).\n- Voicebox running for stage 5. Node on PATH.\n\n## Verification\n- **Per-phase**: `LONGVIEW_WORKSPACE=longview_v2 python benny_cli.py longview report` — every phase\n  `ok`, no unresolved `phase_error`.\n- **Graph after model**: `get_graph_stats(workspace=\"longview_v2\")` shows Concept + RELATES_TO/\n  SOURCED_FROM.\n- **Graph after enrich** (nexus `execute_cypher`, workspace `longview_v2`): cross-document\n  `RELATES_TO {predicate:'semantically_similar'}` > 0; `r.rel_class` populated; concepts with\n  `category` > 0; `merge_count > 1` nodes present — mirrors the v1 longview outcome (563 links /\n  60 themes / 213 merges) at v2's own scale.\n- **Book**: `THE-AI-VAMPIRE.md` (non-trivial) + `.pdf` exist; spot-check a claim cites a session id.\n- **Audiobook**: `02_run_kokoro.py --status` all chapters OK; `build/THE-AI-VAMPIRE.wav` + cue sheet.\n- **Bridge**: open Documents on `longview_v2` — connected, theme-coloured graph with recurring\n  concepts as the largest nodes.\n\n## Risks / guardrails\n- **Never run a deep-synthesis ingest concurrently with reduce/opus** (Lemonade wedge → 0-byte\n  deliverables) — the single sequential `longview run` respects this.\n- Lemonade/Neo4j stability (both wedged/crashed earlier) — phase isolation + resume make restarts\n  cheap; monitor `longview status`.\n- Full backlog is long (guide reference ~52 cards/hr map + per-doc synthesis) — the pilot slice\n  (step 2) proves the model/gate before committing the hours.\n","userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f5cf6c1b-eeb2-4c61-86b9-cd0cc2171896","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16","sessionId":"4cd9df3b-c431-4ac3-8790-b88862