{"parentUuid":"091905bb-4878-4c18-b812-846d83d43848","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_01WJRWy7zHaYjBQckSuiUY8F","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014SuqiGWqX8QWwnHuAD2Fa9","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\.claude\\plans\\warm-beaming-pretzel.md","content":"# LONGVIEW v2 quality pass — lossless meaning flow, enterprise determinism, cohesive book\n\n## Context\n\nReview of the full v2 flow (cards → graph → weave → enrich → review → reduce → opus → pdf) after the\ngraph-walk pilot (6/6 cards, rich content) found five places where context/concepts/meaning **leak or\nare never consumed**, plus determinism gaps. Goal: every distilled signal flows forward losslessly, the\npipeline is reproducible and gated (enterprise-grade), and the book reads as one cohesive journey with\nreflections — an outcome greater than the sum of the parts.\n\n**Findings (verified in code):**\n1. **Concepts leak at ingest.** Cards now carry a high-quality `concepts` list (from per-window walk),\n   but `renderCardMd` (longview.mjs ~447) renders only 3 H2 sections — concepts/evidence never reach\n   the graph; deep-synthesis re-derives concepts from prose (a second lossy LLM pass).\n2. **`operator_traits` is always empty.** The window-fragment prompt doesn't ask for it, yet reduce\n   builds the operator profile from it. (Also feeds \"reflections\" poorly.)\n3. **Review notes are orphaned.** `data_out/reviews/*.md` (the \"greater than the sum\" pass) are written\n   but consumed by nothing — not ingested, not in reduce inputs, not retrievable by opus sections.\n4. **No chronological spine.** The opus outline gets THEMES + dossier *names* only (opus.mjs ~32). The\n   \"whole journey\" needs the arc: cards have `period` (YYYY-MM) but no timeline is ever built.\n5. **No reflections in the book contract.** vampire prompts produce narrative sections; nothing\n   guarantees reflective interludes.\n6. **Determinism gaps:** `loadCards()`/dossier/review reads use fs order (not sorted); temperatures\n   vary per attempt; the section craft rules (2–5 citations, 650–950 words) are asked of the model but\n   **never validated**; no run-config snapshot ties a run to model/ctx/budgets/commit.\n\n## Approach (in pipeline order)\n\n### A. Lossless concept flow into the graph\n- `window_fragment.md`: add `operator_traits` (0–2) to the fragment schema; assembly maps it (drop the\n  hardcoded `[]` in `assembleCard`).\n- `renderCardMd`: add a 4th section `## Concepts and evidence` listing `concepts` (the walk-extracted\n  entities) + `evidence`. Deep synthesis then anchors triples on the *already-distilled* concepts\n  instead of re-guessing from prose. (Stays within the 10-section/doc synthesis cap — 4 H2s.)\n\n### B. Chronological spine (deterministic, no LLM)\n- In `runReduce`, before dossiers: build `data_out/TIMELINE.md` purely in code — cards sorted by\n  (`period`, `session_id`), grouped by month: project, intent one-liner, top outcomes/decisions with\n  (sid) citations. Deterministic input → identical every run.\n- Feed `TIMELINE.md` (clipped) into: dossier calls, THEMES call, and the opus outline + per-part\n  chapter-spec calls (`opus.mjs` corpusBrief) — the book now knows the arc of the journey.\n\n### C. Weave reviews in (the \"greater than the sum\" material)\n- After the `review` phase writes notes: batch-ingest `data_out/reviews/*.md` (vectors; reuse\n  `ingestBatch` with `deepSynthesis:false` — cheap) so `evidenceFor()` retrieval surfaces them to opus\n  sections and weave loops.\n- `runReduce` THEMES input: append the N most recent review notes (clipped) — themes now reflect\n  cross-session collation, not just cards.\n\n### D. Reflections in the book contract\n- `vampire_outline.md`: require each part to end with a **Reflection chapter/section** (\"what this part\n  of the journey taught — grounded in review notes and themes\"), and a closing chapter that reflects on\n  the whole arc. Outline JSON gains `reflection: true` markers (validated in `realParts`).\n- `opus.mjs` section loop: for reflection sections, retrieval query prefixes \"reflection lessons learned\"\n  and the evidence pack includes that part's period-matching review notes (deterministic selection by\n  period), so reflections are grounded in the collation pass, not invented.\n\n### E. Enterprise determinism + gates\n- **Sorted inputs everywhere:** `loadCards()` sorts by (`period`,`session_id`); dossier/review/dir reads\n  sorted; `graphCatalog` results sorted before clipping.\n- **Fixed temperatures:** map fragments 0.2 (already), intent 0.3, outline/sections pinned (0.4\n  constant, retry 0.3) — no attempt-dependent drift beyond documented retry.\n- **Section gate (deterministic validator in `opus.mjs`):** after each section: 400–1,200 words AND ≥2\n  inline citations (`(sid:|concept:|doc:)` regex). Fail → one retry quoting the violation → ledger\n  `ok:false` + keep the better attempt (never a hole in the book).\n- **Run-config snapshot:** at `run` start, ledger a `run_config` entry: git commit, model id, live ctx\n  probe (query lemonade), all budgets, workspace. A book is then attributable to an exact configuration.\n- **Coverage report (deterministic):** after opus assembly write `data_out/opus/COVERAGE.md` + ledger:\n  % of session cards cited, dossiers referenced, sections passing the gate, reflection count. Thresholds\n  in the manifest (`opus.min_citation_coverage`, default 0.35) — below threshold = `phase_error` note,\n  non-fatal, honest.\n\n### F. Prerequisite + execution\n- flm 16k restart still pending (recipe_options.json staged; restart was deferred). After approval:\n  stop `flm.exe` (Lemonade JIT-respawns at 16384), verify cmdline + a >4k-token probe call, then run\n  the full v2 pipeline with the new budgets (.env already staged).\n\n### Critical files\n- `scripts/longview/prompts/window_fragment.md`, `vampire_outline.md` (+`vampire_chapter_sections.md`\n  if section specs need the reflection flag)\n- `scripts/longview/longview.mjs` — assembleCard traits, renderCardMd concepts, TIMELINE build,\n  reviews ingest+reduce input, loadCards sort, run_config ledger\n- `scripts/longview/lib/opus.mjs` — corpusBrief timeline, reflection sections, section gate, coverage\n- `scripts/longview/lib/retrieve.mjs` — sorted graphCatalog (one-line)\n- `runtime/manifests/templates/longview_synthesis.json` — coverage thresholds on the opus phase\n\n## Verification\n- Unit-ish: TIMELINE.md byte-identical across two builds from the same cards; loadCards order stable.\n- Re-map 1 pilot session (`--force --limit 1`): card has non-empty `operator_traits`; its rollup doc\n  shows the `## Concepts and evidence` section.\n- Reduce on pilot cards: TIMELINE.md exists, months ordered; THEMES input includes review notes (log).\n- Opus on the pilot corpus (limit a part): every section passes the citation/word gate or is ledgered;\n  reflection sections present per part; COVERAGE.md written with real percentages.\n- Ledger head has `run_config` with commit + ctx=16384 (post-restart).\n- Then: full 223-session v2 run → book + PDF → Kokoro audiobook (prior plan stands).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1592,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2700,"cache_read_input_tokens":482296,"output_tokens":2866,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2700},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1592,"output_tokens":2866,"cache_read_input_tokens":482296,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2700,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2700,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CcgrUkv1tGpCXj2PoEPP6","type":"assistant","uuid":"757fba96-0596-435a-9f80-