view` + register both dispatch sites (mirror the `enrich` wiring already added)","-- `scripts/longview/lib/gate.mjs` — reuse `validateCard`; add a light fragment validator","-- `scripts/longview/lib/config.mjs` — window/fragment/review knobs","-- `scripts/longview/lib/retrieve.mjs` — reuse for the review pass","-- `runtime/manifests/templates/longview_synthesis.json` — add `review` phase","+- `scripts/longview/prompts/window_fragment.md`, `vampire_outline.md` (+`vampire_chapter_sections.md`","+  if section specs need the reflection flag)","+- `scripts/longview/longview.mjs` — assembleCard traits, renderCardMd concepts, TIMELINE build,","+  reviews ingest+reduce input, loadCards sort, run_config ledger","+- `scripts/longview/lib/opus.mjs` — corpusBrief timeline, reflection sections, section gate, coverage","+- `scripts/longview/lib/retrieve.mjs` — sorted graphCatalog (one-line)","+- `runtime/manifests/templates/longview_synthesis.json` — coverage thresholds on the opus phase"," "," ## Verification","-- **Walk unit test**: on a 1000+-step session, assert Σ(window step counts) == timeline length (every","-  step covered exactly once) and window order is deterministic across two runs; each window ≤ budget.","-- **Pilot**: `LONGVIEW_WORKSPACE=longview_v2 map --limit 5` → **ok=5/5**, including the previously","-  failing `b708c23f`; assert the cards have populated `decisions/outcomes/failures` (no empty lists","-  from lossy repair).","-- **Fidelity spot-check**: compare a graph-walk card vs the old single-call card for one large session","-  — fuller lists, citations intact.","-- **Resume**: interrupt map mid-session, rerun → cached windows are skipped (queue shrinks by completed","-  windows, not whole sessions).","-- **Review**: `review` phase writes `data_out/reviews/*.md` citing graph concepts + cross-session links.","-- **End to end**: full `longview run` on `longview_v2` completes through `pdf`; then the book + Kokoro","-  audiobook per the prior plan.","-","-## Sequencing","-Build + pilot this **before** the full v2 run, so the whole corpus is extracted losslessly. The","-`enrich` phase (committed `47b6f11`) and the memo-ray source fix (`6e56b9c` + `.env`) stay as-is; this","-replaces only the extraction path (`map`) and adds `review`.","+- Unit-ish: TIMELINE.md byte-identical across two builds from the same cards; loadCards order stable.","+- Re-map 1 pilot session (`--force --limit 1`): card has non-empty `operator_traits`; its rollup doc","+  shows the `## Concepts and evidence` section.","+- Reduce on pilot cards: TIMELINE.md exists, months ordered; THEMES input includes review notes (log).","+- Opus on the pilot corpus (limit a part): every section passes the citation/word gate or is ledgered;","+  reflection sections present per part; COVERAGE.md written with real percentages.","+- Ledger head has `run_config` with commit + ctx=16384 (post-restart).","+- Then: full 223-session v2 run → book + PDF → Kokoro audiobook (prior plan stands)."]}],"originalFile":"# LONGVIEW graph-walk extraction — lossless cards + post-graph session review\n\n## Context\n\nThe v2 map pilot exposed a hard limit: qwen3.5-9b-FLM **self-limits its output to ~415 tokens\nregardless of `max_tokens`** — proven by diagnostic (`finish_reason=\"stop\"`, not `\"length\"`, at\n414–419 completion tokens for json, free-form, and max=2000 alike). The LONGVIEW session card has\n**12 fields** (`session_card.md`), which doesn't fit in ~415 tokens, so the model either truncates\nmid-object or closes early with fields missing. The gate (`gate.mjs`) then rejects it\n(pilot: `b708c23f` lost `decisions/outcomes/failures`). `repairTruncatedJson` makes the JSON\nparseable but **discards the dropped content** — lossy. On top of that, `buildEvidencePack`\n(`evidence.mjs`) caps input at **7,500 chars**, so long / 1000+-step sessions lose content before\nthe model ever sees it.\n\n**The user's fix (correct):** walk each session's timeline graph *deterministically and completely*\nin short windows, extract a tiny fragment per window (never near the ~415-token limit), assemble the\ncard **losslessly** in code, then add a dedicated pass that re-visits each session against the built\nconcept graph to collate across sessions — \"greater than the sum of the parts\" without context loss.\n\n**Decisions (user):** per-window = compact card fragments assembled losslessly (concepts still reach\nthe graph via the existing model phase over complete cards); **the walk must be deterministic over\nevery step** (some sessions exceed 1000 steps — none may be skipped); **add a dedicated post-graph\nsession-review phase**.\n\n## Approach\n\n### 1. Deterministic complete graph walk — `scripts/longview/lib/walk.mjs` (new)\n`walkSessionWindows(session, { inputChars })`: `readTimeline(session.id)` (`store.mjs`) already returns\n**every** step entity in deterministic order (BFS over `children_ids` + timestamp sort). Chunk that\nfull ordered list into windows each ≤ `inputChars` (default ~7,000 — sized to fit qwen3.5's 4,096-token\nctx with room for the tiny fragment output). Every step lands in exactly one window; carry the step\nindex range per window for traceability. No sampling, no 7,500-char cap — a 1000-step session becomes\n~N ordered windows, all covered.\n\n### 2. Tiny per-window fragment — `prompts/window_fragment.md` (new)\nCompact schema — short lists (0–4 each): `decisions, outcomes, failures, capabilities, applications,\nartifacts, concepts, open_threads` + `evidence` names, grounded in that window only. Small output stays\nwell inside the ~415-token comfort zone → no truncation. `repairTruncatedJson` remains a per-fragment\nsafety net, now rarely needed.\n\n### 3. Rework `map` (longview.mjs `runMap`) — walk → fragments → lossless assembly\nPer session: for each window → `chat(fragment)` → **cache to `<state>/windows/<sid>/<n>.json`**\n(resume-safe per window — essential for 1000-step sessions so a restart never re-runs completed\nwindows). Then assemble the 12-field card **deterministically**: union + dedup the fragment lists (cap\n0–6 each), derive `period` from timestamps, set `project` from the session/most-common fragment project;\none **tiny** LLM call for `intent` (1–3 sentences) over the merged highlights. Validate with the\nexisting `validateCard` (`gate.mjs`) + write the card. No large JSON is ever generated by the model.\n\n### 4. New `review` phase — `runReview` + `prompts/session_review.md` (new)\nRuns **after `enrich`, before `reduce`** (graph + cross-doc links + themes exist). For each session,\npull its graph neighbourhood — the session's `SOURCED_FROM` concepts, their `RELATES_TO`/\n`semantically_similar` links, and top related concepts via `retrieve.mjs` (`graphCatalog`,\n`evidenceFor`) — and write a graph-grounded review note to `data_out/reviews/<sid>.md` that collates\nthe session's contribution *in the context of the whole corpus*. Ledgered `phase:\"review\"`, resume per\nsession. This is the dedicated \"review sessions after the graph exists\" pass.\n\n### 5. Config + manifest\n`config.mjs`: `WINDOW_INPUT_CHARS` (~7000), `FRAGMENT_MAX_TOKENS` (~400), `REVIEW_INPUT_CHARS`.\n`longview_synthesis.json`: add `{ \"id\": \"review\", \"enabled\": true }` after `enrich`. Final order:\n`inventory → extract → map(walk) → model → code → weave → enrich → review → reduce → opus → pdf`.\n\n### Critical files\n- `scripts/longview/lib/walk.mjs` (new) — deterministic complete windowing over `readTimeline`\n- `scripts/longview/prompts/window_fragment.md`, `prompts/session_review.md` (new)\n- `scripts/longview/longview.mjs` — rewrite `runMap` (walk + fragment + lossless assemble), add\n  `runReview` + register both dispatch sites (mirror the `enrich` wiring already added)\n- `scripts/longview/lib/gate.mjs` — reuse `validateCard`; add a light fragment validator\n- `scripts/longview/lib/config.mjs` — window/fragment/review knobs\n- `scripts/longview/lib/retrieve.mjs` — reuse for the review pass\n- `runtime/manifests/templates/longview_synthesis.json` — add `review` phase\n\n## Verification\n- **Walk unit test**: on a 1000+-step session, assert Σ(window step counts) == timeline length (every\n  step covered exactly once) and window order is deterministic across two runs; each window ≤ budget.\n- **Pilot**: `LONGVIEW_WORKSPACE=longview_v2 map --limit 5` → **ok=5/5**, including the previously\n  failing `b708c23f`; assert the cards have populated `decisions/outcomes/failures` (no empty lists\n  from lossy repair).\n- **Fidelity spot-check**: compare a graph-walk card vs the old single-call card for one large session\n  — fuller lists, citations intact.\n- **Resume**: interrupt map mid-session, rerun → cached windows are skipped (queue shrinks by completed\n  windows, not whole sessions).\n- **Review**: `review` phase writes `data_out/reviews/*.md` citing graph concepts + cross-session links.\n- **End to end**: full `longview run` on `longview_v2` completes through `pdf`; then the book + Kokoro\n  audiobook per the prior plan.\n\n## Sequencing\nBuild + pilot this **before** the full v2 run, so the whole corpus is extracted losslessly. The\n`enrich` phase (committed `47b6f11`) and the memo-ray source fix (`6e56b9c` + `.env`) stay as-is; this\nreplaces only the extraction path (`map`) and adds `review`.\n","userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"757fba96-0596-435a-9f80-a736d8f9cba2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo","sessionId":"4cd9df3b-c431-4ac3-8790-b888629655bb","version":"2.1.197","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"warm-beaming-pretzel"}
