{"parentUuid":"107fefde-0696-4217-994f-1bc2acb2a729","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\.claude\\projects\\C--Users-nsdha-OneDrive-binary16\\memory\\longview_v2_graph_walk_pipeline.md","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\.claude\\projects\\C--Users-nsdha-OneDrive-binary16\\memory\\longview_v2_graph_walk_pipeline.md","content":"---\nname: longview-v2-graph-walk-pipeline\ndescription: \"LONGVIEW v2 overhaul: graph-walk lossless extraction (qwen3.5 415-token self-limit), 16k FLM ctx, enrich+review phases, book gates/reflections/coverage, workspace-precedence bug\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 4cd9df3b-c431-4ac3-8790-b888629655bb\n---\n\n2026-07-04, LONGVIEW v2 clean-room run (workspace `longview_v2`, 224 sessions) — the pipeline was overhauled for lossless extraction + enterprise determinism. See [[longview_memoray_source_fix]], [[prime_silo_longview_graph_enrichment]], [[project_longview_session_synthesis]].\n\n**qwen3.5-9b-FLM self-limits output to ~415 tokens** regardless of max_tokens (`finish_reason:\"stop\"` at 414–419 for json/free-form/max=2000 alike — proven by diagnostic). A 12-field session card can't fit → truncated/missing fields; `repairTruncatedJson` salvages syntax but LOSES content. Raising ctx does NOT fix output; it fixes INPUT.\n\n**Graph-walk extraction (commit 4e393cf):** `scripts/longview/lib/walk.mjs` deterministically windows the FULL session timeline (readTimeline; every step covered once — verified 4,999 steps → 534 windows; over-long steps split across windows). map extracts a tiny per-window fragment (`prompts/window_fragment.md`, cached `windows/<sid>/w<chars>_<n>.json` — size-keyed, resume-safe) and **assembles the card losslessly in code** (union/dedup + one small intent call). Pilot: 1/5 ok → **6/6 ok** incl. previously-truncated sessions.\n\n**16k ctx (live):** `~/.cache/lemonade/recipe_options.json` per-model override `\"qwen3.5-9b-FLM\": {\"ctx_size\": 16384}`; restart = kill flm.exe + `POST /api/v1/load {\"model_name\":\"qwen3.5-9b-FLM\"}` (a chat call right after the kill races the respawn — use /load). Verified cmdline `--ctx-len 16384` + a 14,413-token prompt accepted. Antigravity RAM math confirmed (+1.6GB at 16k; 7.3GB free). `.env`: LONGVIEW_WINDOW_CHARS=24000, LONGVIEW_EVIDENCE_BUDGET=20000, LONGVIEW_REDUCE_INPUT=24000 → map ETA 21h → ~6h.\n\n**Quality pass (commit d938448)** — closes the \"leaks\" so the outcome exceeds the sum of parts:\n- renderCardMd 4th H2 `## Concepts and evidence` → deep synthesis anchors on walk-extracted concepts (was re-deriving from prose). Note: model phase skips re-render if data_in doc exists.\n- Fragments extract `operator_traits` (was hardcoded [] though reduce builds the operator profile from it).\n- Deterministic `data_out/TIMELINE.md` (cards sorted period+sid, no LLM) → themes + opus outline/chapters; outline prompt mandates chronological journey with resolution.\n- `review` phase notes ingested as vectors + appended to themes input (were orphaned).\n- **Reflection chapters code-enforced** per part (deterministic single section, grounded in reviewsDigest) — never asked of the model.\n- Gates: sectionGate validates 400–1300 words + ≥2 `(sid:|concept:|doc:)` citations, one retry, keeps best draft, ledgers gate_errors; `COVERAGE.md` (% sessions cited vs cards, threshold LONGVIEW_OPUS_MIN_CITE_COVERAGE=0.35, warn not fatal); `run_config` ledger entry (git commit, model, ctx from recipe_options, budgets, phases).\n- Sorted reads everywhere (loadCards by period+sid, dossiers/reviews sorted).\n\n**CRITICAL BUG caught live (commit c01ea97):** the manifest's hardcoded `\"workspace\": \"longview\"` **unconditionally overrode** `LONGVIEW_WORKSPACE` env — the v2 run silently started against production `longview` (killed at extract; graph untouched; longview's inventory.json now lists 224 sessions — harmless for delta). Fix: env wins when explicitly set. **Always verify the `[run] … → workspace 'X'` log line after launch.**\n\n**Benny Record (commit f45b0cc) — observability layer.** Provenance capture at every seam: `evidenceForWithSources` (retrieve.mjs) persists which chunks/concepts fed each opus section (`sections/<id>.meta.json` incl. cited sids/concepts/gate/tokens); `reduceCall` writes `<out>.meta.json`; map writes `windows/<sid>/manifest.json` (window→step ranges) + `cards/<sid>.meta.json` (card readers must exclude `.meta.json`!). `lib/record.mjs`: `recordFor(scope)` = captioned action timeline from ledger+meta (step_through shape); `lineageFor(scope)` = tree deliverable→evidence→card→windows→session raw log path (+concept nodes). CLI `longview record <scope> [--json]`; APIs `GET /api/longview_record?scope=` + `GET /api/longview_ledger?since=<line>` (append-only tail + heartbeat = live telemetry feed) via longview_service. Verified live on card:b4e58880 — full honest history incl. its earlier gate failure, down to the raw `.jsonl` log. **TODO: the player UI** (`app/L0/.../benny_record/` forked from step_through: scrubber/hero/why + lineage map + live tail + gate chips/token meter + cross-jump to step_through; Bridge ▶ Record buttons) — plan in ~/.claude/plans/warm-beaming-pretzel.md.\n\n**Pipeline now:** inventory → extract → map(walk) → model → code → weave → enrich → **review** → reduce(TIMELINE) → opus(reflections+gates+coverage) → pdf. Full v2 run launched (background, day-scale, resume-safe; `longview status` / Bridge → Documents on longview_v2). Next after completion: verify graph/enrich/review, book + COVERAGE, then Kokoro audiobook (`LONGVIEW_BOOK_DIR=<home>/workspaces/longview_v2/data_out/opus`, 01_prepare→02_run_kokoro→03_stitch). Uncommitted-to-release: everything since v1.11.4 (commits 4e393cf, d938448, c01ea97, 47b6f11, 6e56b9c, a900605 on main — no tag yet).\n","numLines":32,"startLine":1,"totalLines":32}},"displayPath":"..\\..\\.claude\\projects\\C--Users-nsdha-OneDrive-binary16\\memory\\longview_v2_graph_walk_pipeline.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"a6cbe2e4-d8d1-4449-aa53-8a87785f10b0","timestamp":"2026-07-04T23:04:05.043Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16","sessionId":"4cd9df3b-c431-4ac3-8790-b888629655bb","version":"2.1.197","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"warm-beaming-pretzel"}
{"parentUuid":"a6cbe2e4-d8d1-4449-aa53-8a87785f10b0","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo\\server\\api\\longview_ledger.js","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo\\server\\api\\longview_ledger.js","content":"// GET /api/longview_ledger?since=<line>[&workspace=longview_v2]\n//\n// Incremental tail of the runner's append-only ledger.jsonl + the status.json\n// heartbeat — the real-time telemetry feed. Poll with the returned `next` as\n// the following `since`; the response contains only new entries, so a live\n// Benny Record view (or telemetry strip) costs one cheap read per tick.\nimport longviewService from \"../../packaging/desktop/longview_service.js\";\n\nexport const allowAnonymous = false;\n\nexport function get(context) {\n  const since = Number(context.params?.since || 0) || 0;\n  const workspace = context.params?.workspace;\n  return {\n    headers: { \"Cache-Control\": \"no-store\" },\n    status: 200,\n    body: longviewService.longviewLedger({ since, ...(workspace ? { workspace } : {}) })\n  };\n}\n","numLines":20,"startLine":1,"totalLines":20}},"displayPath":"prime-silo\\server\\api\\longview_ledger.js"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"21a3ca6a-e400-4cd1-8458-747e22d97636","timestamp":"2026-07-04T23:04:04.636Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16","sessionId":"4cd9df3b-c431-4ac3-8790-b888629655bb","version":"2.1.197","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"warm-beaming-pretzel"}
{"parentUuid":"21a3ca6a-e400-4cd1-8458-747e22d97636","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo\\server\\api\\longview_record.js","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo\\server\\api\\longview_record.js","content":"// GET /api/longview_record?scope=card:<sid8>|section:<id>|dossier:<n>|book|run\n//                          [&workspace=longview_v2]\n//\n// Benny Record: the full provenance of an output — an ordered, human-captioned\n// action timeline (every LLM call, gate verdict, ingest) plus the lineage tree\n// (deliverable → evidence → cards → windows → source session log). Read-only,\n// disk-backed (ledger + meta files), assembled by scripts/longview/lib/record.mjs.\nimport longviewService from \"../../packaging/desktop/longview_service.js\";\n\nexport const allowAnonymous = false;\n\nexport function get(context) {\n  const scope = String(context.params?.scope || \"run\");\n  const workspace = context.params?.workspace;\n  return {\n    headers: { \"Cache-Control\": \"no-store\" },\n    status: 200,\n    body: longviewService.longviewRecord({ scope, ...(workspace ? { workspace } : {}) })\n  };\n}\n","numLines":21,"startLine":1,"totalLines":21}},"displayPath":"prime-silo\\server\\api\\longview_record.js"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"910c9972-2889-4d2f-8053-8cfdb7ab72cf","timestamp":"2026-07-04T23:04:04.705Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16","sessionId":"4cd9df3b-c431-4ac3-8790-b888629655bb","version":"2.1.197","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"warm-beaming-pretzel"}
{"parentUuid":"910c9972-2889-4d2f-8053-8cfdb7ab72cf","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"compact_file_reference","filename":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo\\scripts\\longview\\longview.mjs","displayPath":"prime-silo\\scripts\\longview\\longview.mjs"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"8c0d1a99-5718-4cfd-a170-5740e56c8a96","timestamp":"2026-07-04T23:04:05.045Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16","sessionId":"4cd9df3b-c431-4ac3-8790-b888629655bb","version":"2.1.197","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"warm-beaming-pretzel"}
{"parentUuid":"8c0d1a99-5718-4cfd-a170-5740e56c8a96","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo\\scripts\\longview\\lib\\record.mjs","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo\\scripts\\longview\\lib\\record.mjs","content":"// Benny Record (ADR-005 observability) — turn the pipeline's audit trail\n// (ledger.jsonl + provenance meta files + window manifests + memo-ray store)\n// into (a) an ordered, human-captioned action timeline (the step_through shape)\n// and (b) a lineage tree for the map pane. Deterministic: sorted inputs only.\nimport fs from \"fs\";\nimport path from \"path\";\nimport { config, workspaceDir, stateDir } from \"./config.mjs\";\nimport { readLedger } from \"./ledger.mjs\";\n\nconst readJson = (p) => {\n  try {\n    return JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(p, \"utf8\"));\n  } catch {\n    return null;\n  }\n};\nconst sid8 = (id) => String(id).slice(0, 8);\n\nfunction caption(e) {\n  if (e.action === \"run_config\") return `Run pinned: commit ${e.git_commit}, model ${e.model}, ctx ${e.ctx_size}`;\n  if (e.phase === \"map\" && e.status === \"ok\") return `Mapped session ${sid8(e.session_id)} into a card (${e.retries ? \"retry\" : \"clean\"}, ${Math.round((e.ms || 0) / 1000)}s)`;\n  if (e.phase === \"map\" && e.status === \"failed\") return `Card for ${sid8(e.session_id)} failed the gate: ${(e.gate_errors || []).join(\"; \").slice(0, 120)}`;\n  if (e.phase === \"review\" && e.status === \"ok\") return `Reviewed ${sid8(e.session_id)} against the graph (${(e.related_concepts || []).length} cross-session concepts)`;\n  if (e.phase === \"opus\" && /^section:/.test(e.artifact || \"\")) return `${e.ok === false ? \"Draft kept but gate-failed\" : \"Wrote\"} book ${e.artifact} (${e.words || \"?\"} words, ${e.citations ?? \"?\"} citations)`;\n  if (e.phase === \"opus\" && e.artifact === \"coverage\") return `Book coverage: ${Math.round((e.citation_coverage || 0) * 100)}% of sessions cited`;\n  if (e.action === \"phase_error\") return `Phase ${e.phase} errored (isolated): ${String(e.error || \"\").slice(0, 100)}`;\n  if (e.artifact) return `Produced ${e.artifact}${e.ok === false ? \" (FAILED)\" : \"\"}`;\n  return `${e.phase || \"step\"}: ${e.status || e.action || \"event\"}`;\n}\n\nconst WHY = {\n  map: \"Distill each session's timeline into a gated card via short graph-walk windows.\",\n  model: \"Ingest cards into the knowledge graph (deep synthesis).\",\n  code: \"Scan the repo into the code graph and correlate it to concepts.\",\n  weave: \"Ask what is under-explored; answer from retrieval; re-ingest the notes.\",\n  enrich: \"Merge duplicate concepts, add cross-document links, type relations, name themes.\",\n  review: \"Re-visit each session against the built graph — the collation pass.\",\n  reduce: \"Fold cards into dossiers, themes, timeline and reports.\",\n  opus: \"Write the book: retrieval-grounded, gated, cited sections.\",\n  pdf: \"Typeset the assembled book.\",\n  run: \"Pin the run to an exact configuration.\"\n};\n\nexport function recordFor(scope) {\n  const ledger = readLedger();\n  const [kind, ref] = scope.includes(\":\") ? scope.split(\":\", 2) : [scope, null];\n  const match = (e) => {\n    if (kind === \"run\") return true;\n    if (kind === \"card\") return String(e.session_id || \"\").startsWith(ref);\n    if (kind === \"review\") return e.phase === \"review\" && String(e.session_id || \"\").startsWith(ref);\n    if (kind === \"section\") return e.artifact === `section:${ref}`;\n    if (kind === \"book\") return e.phase === \"opus\" || e.phase === \"pdf\";\n    if (kind === \"dossier\") return String(e.artifact || \"\").startsWith(`dossier:${ref}`);\n    return false;\n  };\n  const actions = ledger.filter(match).map((e, i) => ({\n    n: i,\n    type: e.action || e.phase || \"event\",\n    caption: caption(e),\n    why: WHY[e.phase] || WHY[e.action] || \"\",\n    content: e,\n    ts: e.ts || null,\n    ms: e.ms || null,\n    tokens: (e.prompt_tokens || 0) + (e.completion_tokens || 0) || null,\n    nodeId: e.session_id ? `card:${sid8(e.session_id)}` : e.artifact ? `art:${e.artifact}` : `phase:${e.phase}`\n  }));\n  return { scope, workspace: config.WORKSPACE, actions };\n}\n\nexport function lineageFor(scope) {\n  const [kind, ref] = scope.includes(\":\") ? scope.split(\":\", 2) : [scope, null];\n  const nodes = [];\n  const links = [];\n  const seen = new Set();\n  const add = (id, type, label, depth, meta = {}) => {\n    if (!seen.has(id)) {\n      seen.add(id);\n      nodes.push({ id, type, label, depth, meta });\n    }\n    return id;\n  };\n  const link = (a, b) => links.push({ source: a, target: b });\n\n  const cardLineage = (sidPrefix, depth) => {\n    const dir = stateDir(\"cards\");\n    const f = (fs.existsSync(dir) ? fs.readdirSync(dir) : []).find(\n      (x) => x.startsWith(sidPrefix) && x.endsWith(\".json\") && !x.endsWith(\".meta.json\")\n    );\n    if (!f) return null;\n    const sid = f.replace(/\\.json$/, \"\");\n    const card = readJson(path.join(dir, f)) || {};\n    const cardId = add(`card:${sid8(sid)}`, \"Card\", `${card.project || \"card\"} (${sid8(sid)})`, depth, {\n      meta: readJson(path.join(dir, `${sid}.meta.json`))\n    });\n    const man = readJson(stateDir(\"windows\", sid, \"manifest.json\"));\n    if (man) {\n      const wId = add(`windows:${sid8(sid)}`, \"Windows\", `${man.windows.length} windows over ${man.step_count} steps`, depth + 1, man);\n      link(cardId, wId);\n    }\n    const entity = readJson(path.join(config.MEMORAY_DATA_DIR, \"entities\", `${sid}.json`));\n    const sesId = add(`session:${sid8(sid)}`, \"Session\", entity ? `${entity.agent}: ${(entity.content || \"\").slice(0, 60)}` : `session ${sid8(sid)}`, depth + 2, {\n      session_id: sid,\n      log_path: entity?.metadata?.filePath || null\n    });\n    link(cardId, sesId);\n    return cardId;\n  };\n\n  if (kind === \"card\" || kind === \"review\") {\n    add(`root:${scope}`, \"Artifact\", scope, 0);\n    const c = cardLineage(ref, 1);\n    if (c) link(`root:${scope}`, c);\n  } else if (kind === \"section\") {\n    const meta = readJson(workspaceDir(\"data_out\", \"opus\", \"sections\", `${ref}.meta.json`)) || {};\n    const rootId = add(`section:${ref}`, \"Section\", `§${ref}`, 0, meta);\n    for (const s of meta.evidence_sources || []) {\n      if (s.kind === \"graph\") {\n        const cId = add(`concept:${s.source}`, \"Concept\", s.source, 1, {});\n        link(rootId, cId);\n      } else {\n        const m = String(s.source || \"\").match(/longview_(?:card|review)_([a-z0-9]{8})/i);\n        if (m) {\n          const c = cardLineage(m[1], 2);\n          const eId = add(`doc:${s.source}`, \"Evidence\", s.source, 1, {});\n          link(rootId, eId);\n          if (c) link(eId, c);\n        } else {\n          link(rootId, add(`doc:${s.source}`, \"Evidence\", String(s.source), 1, {}));\n        }\n      }\n    }\n    for (const sid of meta.cited_sids || []) {\n      const c = cardLineage(sid, 2);\n      if (c) link(rootId, c);\n    }\n    for (const con of meta.cited_concepts || []) link(rootId, add(`concept:${con}`, \"Concept\", con, 1, {}));\n  } else if (kind === \"dossier\") {\n    const p = workspaceDir(\"data_out\", \"dossiers\", `${ref}.md`);\n    const rootId = add(`dossier:${ref}`, \"Dossier\", ref, 0, readJson(p + \".meta.json\") || {});\n    const dir = stateDir(\"cards\");\n    for (const f of (fs.existsSync(dir) ? fs.readdirSync(dir) : []).filter((x) => x.endsWith(\".json\") && !x.endsWith(\".meta.json\")).sort()) {\n      const card = readJson(path.join(dir, f)) || {};\n      if (String(card.project || \"\").toLowerCase() === ref.replace(/_/g, \" \").toLowerCase() || String(card.project || \"\").toLowerCase() === ref.toLowerCase()) {\n        const c = cardLineage(f.slice(0, 8), 1);\n        if (c) link(rootId, c);\n      }\n    }\n  } else {\n    // book / run: parts → chapters → sections (lineage per section on demand)\n    const outline = readJson(workspaceDir(\"data_out\", \"opus\", \"outline.json\")) || { parts: [] };\n    const rootId = add(\"book\", \"Book\", outline.title || \"Book\", 0, {});\n    for (const part of outline.parts || []) {\n      const pId = add(`part:${part.n}`, \"Part\", part.title, 1, {});\n      link(rootId, pId);\n      for (const ch of part.chapters || []) {\n        const cId = add(`chapter:${ch.n}`, \"Chapter\", ch.title, 2, { reflection: !!ch.reflection });\n        link(pId, cId);\n        for (const s of ch.sections || []) link(cId, add(`section:${s.id}`, \"Section\", s.title, 3, {}));\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  return { scope, nodes, links };\n}\n","numLines":164,"startLine":1,"totalLines":164}},"displayPath":"prime-silo\\scripts\\longview\\lib\\record.mjs"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"aa7a4967-7068-4b6a-aea8-341e21168608","timestamp":"2026-07-04T23:04:05.046Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16","sessionId":"4cd9df3b-c431-4ac3-8790-b888629655bb","version":"2.1.197","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"warm-beaming-pretzel"}
{"parentUuid":"aa7a4967-7068-4b6a-aea8-341e21168608","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"plan_file_reference","planFilePath":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\.claude\\plans\\warm-beaming-pretzel.md","planContent":"# Benny Record — step-through playback + live telemetry + full output lineage\n\n## Context\n\nThe v2 pipeline has strong *audit* (append-only `ledger.jsonl`, `run_config`, gates, COVERAGE) but\n(1) no real-time view and (2) no way to pick an output and see the whole tree that made it —\nagents, scripts, LLM calls, evidence, graph concepts (\"ontology breadcrumbs\").\n\nmemo-ray already solved the *experience* problem for sessions: the **step_through player**\n(`app/L0/_all/mod/_prime_silo/step_through/step_through.js`) — a calming step-by-step audit: hero\ncaption, the preceding \"Why?\", raw content/diff, milestone scrubber, a lineage map\n(`createLineageGraphWidget`) highlighting the current step, play/pause/speed, keyboard/gamepad,\nspeech narration. It replays *operator↔agent sessions*.\n\n**The idea (user's): a \"Benny Record\"** — the same experience pointed at *Benny's own work*: replay\nhow the pipeline produced any deliverable, step by step, enriched with everything prime-silo knows —\nmodel calls + tokens, evidence retrievals, gate verdicts, graph-concept deltas, phases, commit. And\nbecause the ledger is append-only, **the same player tail-following the live run IS the real-time\ntelemetry view** — one experience for history and now.\n\n**Timing:** v2 is in map. Landing capture before reduce/opus means the v2 book ships fully\nreplayable.\n\n## Approach\n\n### 1. Provenance capture (the missing edges — prerequisite for everything)\n- `lib/retrieve.mjs` `evidenceFor()`: also return `sources[]` (ragQuery already has `r.source`;\n  today discarded).\n- `lib/opus.mjs`: write `sections/<id>.meta.json` — query, evidence sources, cited sids/concepts\n  (regex from final text), attempts, tokens, gate result, model, git commit, ts.\n- `longview.mjs reduceCall`: `<deliverable>.meta.json` (inputs digest + tokens). map: persist\n  `windows/<sid>/manifest.json` (window → step ranges, from `walkSessionWindows`) +\n  `cards/<sid>.meta.json`. review ledger entries gain `{anchors[], related_concepts[]}`.\n\n### 2. The Record — normalizer + lineage assembly (`scripts/longview/lib/record.mjs`, new)\n- `recordFor(scope)` where scope = `run | artifact` (`book | section:<id> | dossier:<n> |\n  card:<sid8> | review:<sid8>`): merge ledger entries + meta files + window manifests + memo-ray\n  store into an **ordered action timeline** in the step_through shape:\n  `{type: phase|llm_call|retrieval|gate|ingest|graph_delta, caption (plain English), why (phase\n  intent), content (prompt/output/evidence heads), ts, ms, tokens, nodeId}`.\n- `lineageFor(artifact)`: the tree for the map pane — deliverable → generation calls → evidence\n  docs → cards → windows → sessions (raw log path) — in `createLineageGraphWidget`'s\n  `{nodes, links}` shape, **joined into the ontology**: cited concepts resolved against Neo4j\n  (name, merge_count, aliases, community) via the graph API.\n- CLI: `node scripts/longview/longview.mjs record <scope> [--json]` (also serves as the terminal\n  breadcrumbs view).\n\n### 3. Server APIs (mirror `server/api/longview_status.js`)\n- `server/api/longview_record.js` — GET `/api/longview_record?scope=…` (timeline + lineage tree).\n- `server/api/longview_ledger.js` — GET `/api/longview_ledger?since=<line>` (incremental tail of\n  ledger.jsonl + status.json) — powers live mode cheaply.\n\n### 4. Benny Record player (`app/L0/_all/mod/_prime_silo/benny_record/`, new — forked thin from\nstep_through, sharing its css patterns + `createLineageGraphWidget`)\n- Same core UX: hero caption (\"Benny retrieved 4 evidence chunks for §p2c4s1\"), \"Why?\" (phase\n  intent), content pane (evidence sources / prompt head / section draft / gate verdict), milestone\n  scrubber, lineage map tracking the current step, play/pause/speed, ←/→.\n- **Prime-silo enrichments** step_through doesn't have: token-burn meter per step, gate chips\n  (pass/GATE-FAIL with errors), graph-delta chips (\"+12 concepts, +3 similarity links\"), model/ctx/\n  commit badge (from `run_config`), phase progress rail.\n- **Live mode**: when the scoped run is active, the player tail-follows `/api/longview_ledger`\n  (auto-advance on new entries; pause to scrub history) — this replaces a separate telemetry\n  dashboard.\n- **Cross-jump**: a card/session step deep-links to the classic memo-ray step_through\n  (`#/_prime_silo/step_through?session_id=…`) — Benny Record shows how the deliverable was made;\n  step_through shows what happened inside the source session. Two players, one continuum.\n- Entry points: Bridge → Documents Outputs rows get **▶ Record**; LONGVIEW panel gets **Live\n  record** while running; deep link `#/_prime_silo/benny_record?scope=…`.\n\n### Critical files\n- capture: `scripts/longview/lib/retrieve.mjs`, `lib/opus.mjs`, `lib/walk.mjs`, `longview.mjs`\n- record: `scripts/longview/lib/record.mjs` (new) + CLI case\n- server: `server/api/longview_record.js`, `server/api/longview_ledger.js` (new)\n- player: `app/L0/_all/mod/_prime_silo/benny_record/` (new; reuse\n  `widgets/memoray/lineage_graph/index.js`, step_through css/UX patterns, activity-store polling)\n- Bridge: `bridge.js`/`view.html` (▶ Record buttons + Live record chip)\n\n## Verification\n- Capture: re-map 1 session → windows manifest + card meta exist; 1 pilot opus section →\n  `sections/<id>.meta.json` lists real evidence sources.\n- CLI: `longview record card:<sid8>` prints an ordered action timeline ending at the raw session\n  log path; `record section:<id>` includes retrieval steps + gate verdict + concept joins.\n- API: `/api/longview_record?scope=card:…` returns timeline+tree; `/api/longview_ledger?since=n`\n  returns strictly-append batches.\n- Player: open `#/_prime_silo/benny_record?scope=card:<sid8>` — scrub, play, map highlights follow;\n  gate chips + token meter render; cross-jump opens step_through on the source session. With the\n  live v2 run: Live record auto-advances as map events land.\n- Determinism: `recordFor`/`lineageFor` twice → identical output (sorted inputs).\n\n## Sequencing\n1 (capture) immediately — before v2 reaches reduce/opus. Then 2→3→4. All additive; the running map\nphase is unaffected.\n"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"9a6109c2-d9a7-4019-adc7-26ae45a2c632","timestamp":"2026-07-04T23:04:05.046Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16","sessionId":"4cd9df3b-c431-4ac3-8790-b888629655bb","version":"2.1.197","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"warm-beaming-pretzel"}
